1 OCCU Roi des Hérules, Roi d'Italie (476-493), Teutonic chieftain, conquered the Roman Empire & became King ofItaly476-493
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Odoacer''' (c.433–493), also known as '''Odovacer''', was the 5th-century King of Italy, whose reign is commonly seen as marking the end of the classical Roman Empire in Western Europe and the beginning of the M
2 CONC iddle Ages. He is considered the first non-Roman to ever have ruled all of Italy.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was son of a barbarian mercenary in Attila's army, perhaps of  '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Edeko-Chief-of-the-Scirii/6000000015965884288 Edeko]'''. He was probably the Odoacer who commanded a group of Saxon pirates who occup
2 CONC ied a group of islands on the Loire and who attacked Angers in 463. He was defeated by the combined efforts of the Franks and Romans, and became a Roman mercenary in 470. In August 475, he offered his support to '''[http://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/people/Orestes/6000000017547603629 Orestes]''' in his conflict against '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Julius-Nepos-Western-Roman-Emperor/6000000017547260935 Emperor Julius Nepos]'''. A year later, he led the mercenary revolt
2 CONC  against Orestes, whom he killed. He then dethroned '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Romulus-Augustulus-Roman-Emperor/6000000017547922757 Romulus Augustulus]''', the last Western Roman Emperor. He was proclaimed king by his own troo
2 CONC ps. He sent the imperial insignia to the Eastern Emperor at Constantinople and received in return recognition as Magister Militum in Italy. After a remarkable reign, he was killed in 493 by '''[http://www.geni.com/family-tree/inde
2 CONC x/6000000000437226378 Theodoric]''', King of the Ostrogoths, after being defeated in the battles of Isonzo, Verona, Adda and Ravenna.
2 CONT
2 CONT His origin is uncertain. He seems to have been son of Edeko, a vassal of the Huns, and he was certainly a brother of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Onoulphus/6000000014132319403 Onoulphus]''', a general of the Eastern Roman Empire
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a reconstruction by Stephan Krautschick, Odoacer and Onoulphus were brothers of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Flavius-Armatus/6000000000316459716 Flavius Armatus]''', so like Armatus, they were probably also nephews 
2 CONC of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Flavius-Basiliscus-Augustus/6000000007167194211 Basiliscus]''' and '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Aelia-Verina/6000000007166533573 Empress Verina]'''. If so, his mother would have been a sister of
2 CONC  Basiliscus and Verina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Odoacer married '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Sunigilda/6000000012385538222 Sunigilda]''', daughter of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Rogus/6000000022173078679 Rogus]'''. He had several children, including '''[http://www.geni.com
2 CONC /people/Thela/6000000022173388022 Thela]'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ITALY,%20Kings%20to%20962.htm#_Toc203638168 Odovacar 476-493] at Foundation for Medieval Genealogy, visited Aug. 22, 2013.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Krautschick, Stephan (1986). "Zwei Aspekte des Jahres 476". Historia 35: pp. 344–371.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Wikipedia: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odoacer English]
