1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Edeko''' was for some time the chief of the Scirii. In the middle of the 5th century the Scirii were a Germanic Tribe and vassals of the Huns. Edeko was a famous person at the court of '''[http://www.geni.com/pe
2 CONC ople/Attila-Scourge-of-God-59th-King-of-the-Huns/6000000000722248117 Attila]'''. According to written sources he protected Attila with his life. In the Battle of Châlons Edeko fought by the side of the Huns.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the destruction of the Sciri, who had been incited to break their treaty with the Ostrogoths by '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Hunimund-Prince-of-the-Suevi/6000000008019616465 Hunimund]''', king of the Swabians, Edeko, w
2 CONC ith his son '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Onoulphus/6000000014132319403 Onoulphus]''', joined the Swabian side in the Battle of Bolia in the late 460s, where they were again defeated by the Ostrogoths under their king '''[http://
2 CONC www.geni.com/people/Theodomir-King-of-the-Ostrogoths/6000000000508474079 Theodemir]'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edeko was the father of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Odoacer-1st-Germanic-King-of-Italy/6000000004257979021 Odoacer]''', who became a ''magister militum'' in the Roman Army and king of Italy.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a reconstruction by Stephan Krautschick, Odoacer and Onoulphus were brothers of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Flavius-Armatus/6000000000316459716 Flavius Armatus]''', so they were also nephews of '''[http://www.geni.
2 CONC com/people/Flavius-Basiliscus-Augustus/6000000007167194211 Basiliscus]''' and '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Aelia-Verina/6000000007166533573 Empress Verina]''' and Edeko must have been married to a sister of Verina.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Krautschick, Stephan (1986). "Zwei Aspekte des Jahres 476". Historia 35: pp. 344–371.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edeko English]
