2 CONT Page 65:
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.  CHLOTHILDE, 475-d. Tours 3 June 548. While in exile she was spotted by enoys of CLOVIS, who had brought to Francia  where he mar. her 493.  An ardent Catholic, she persuaded CLOVIS to adopt her faith.  For her good works she c
2 CONC omes down in Chuch history as St. CHLOTILDE.  Her canonical day is 3 June.
2 CONT They had four sons.
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-2782
