2 CONC ory of Tours names (in order) Theudovald, Gunthar and Chlodovald as the sons of King Chlodomer, specifying that their paternal grandmother took them into her own household after the death of their father[112].  The Liber Historiæ 
2 CONC Francorum records that "filios…Chlodomire orfanos Theudovaldo, Gunthario et Chlodoaldo" were brought up by "Chrodchildis regina" after their father was killed[113].  In a later passage, Gregory records that the two older sons were
2 CONC  murdered by their uncle King Clotaire, who suspected that his mother was plotting for their succession to the throne, specifying that the younger son was 7 years old[114]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#ClovisI
2 CONC B MEDLANDS]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>c)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Chlodoald-Merovingian/6000000037864811488?through=6000000010395927288 CHLODOVALD] [Cloud] ([524]-7 Sep [560], bur Monastery of Saint-Martin [later Saint-Cloud] near Paris).  Gregory of T
2 CONC ours names (in order) Theudovald, Gunthar and Chlodovald as the sons of King Chlodomer, specifying that their paternal grandmother took them into her own household after the death of their father[115].  The Liber Historiæ Francoru
2 CONC m records that "filios…Chlodomire orfanos Theudovaldo, Gunthario et Chlodoaldo" were brought up by "Chrodchildis regina" after their father was killed[116].  In a later passage, Gregory records that Chlodovald escaped the fate of 
2 CONC his brothers and entered a religious life[117].  He became a monk at Nogent (now Saint-Cloud), near Paris, where he founded the monastery of Saint-Martin, renamed Saint-Cloud by the 8th century.   The Vita Sancti Chlodovaldi recor
2 CONC ds the death of Chlodovald on "VII Id Sep" but does not specify the year[118].  He was canonised as St Cloud, feast day 7 Sep[119]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#ClovisIB MEDLANDS]
