2 CONT Sources: RC 303; AF; Kraentzler 1636; Collins; Pfafman; "The Franks" by Edward James; Chart in "Women in the Wall" by Julia O'Faolain.   Franks: Ruled from 511-561. The youngest and last surviving son of Clovis. Founded St. Medard
2 CONC  Church at Soissons.   RC: Clothaire I, King of Soissons, 511; King of Orleans, 524; King of France, 558-561.
2 CONT    K: Clothaire I, King of Franks and of Soissons.
2 CONT    Collins: Clothaire I (pronounced Clotary).   Pfafman: Clothaire I (Lothar I), King of Soissons 511-558. Sole King of the Franks 558-561. Born 499, died 561.   Chart in "Women in the Wall" lists these wives for "Clotair" I: (1) 
2 CONC Guntheuca, (2) Chunsina, (3) Ingunda, (4) Aregunda, (5) Radeguna, (6) a concubine, and (7) Vuldetrada. It lists children for wives 2, 3, 4 and 6.
