2 TITL Childeric I of the Franks - Find A Grave Memorial
1 NOTE From THE RUFUS PARKS PEDIGREE by Brian J.L. Berry,  chart pg 61.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 65:
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.     CHILDÉRIC I, c.436-481; king of the Salic Franks from 458.  His kingcom included lands along the Seine, Marne, Meuse and Moselle and the towns of Tréves (Trier), Angers and Orleans.  The first documented Salic king, his tom
2 CONC b was discovered at Tournai in 1653.  It contained a royal treasure including his seal ring and several gold bees, the imperial emblem of the Merovingians later adopted by Napoleon.  CHILDÉRIC mar. aft. 463 BASINA  dau. of King CH
2 CONC ILPÉRIC of Thuringia.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Karen, Kristen, Kevin, Brian, Amy, Adam and FAL
