1 NOTE {geni:about_me} King Clotaire had one child by Mistress (1):
2 CONT
2 CONT 9.          CHRAMN (-murdered [30 Nov/31 Dec] 560).  Gregory of Tours names Chramn as the son of King Clotaire and his concubine Chunsina[224].  Gregory records that Chramn was hated by the townsfolk of Clermont-Ferrand, where he 
2 CONC lived, for his dissolute way of life, and in a later passage specifies that he moved on to Poitiers where he conspired against his father[225].  Gregory also says that Chramn allied himself with his uncle King Childebert in Paris,
2 CONC  later rebelling once more against his father before fleeing to Brittany, where he and his wife and daughters went into hiding with "Chanao Count of the Bretons" but were captured and murdered[226].   The Marii Episcopi Aventicens
2 CONC is Chronica records that "Cramnus filius Chlothacharii regis" sought a hiding place from "Childeberto patruo suo" in 555[227].  Paulus Diaconus records that "duce Francorum Chramnichis" laid waste to Trentino after defeating a Lom
2 CONC bard invasion of France but was defeated by "Euin Tridentum dux" at "Salurnis"[228].  Gregory of Tours records his father, King Clotaire, died on the first anniversary of the killing of his son Chramn[229].  m CHALDA, daughter of 
2 CONC WILLICHAR & his wife --- (-murdered 560).  Gregory of Tours records that the wife of Chramn was the daughter of Willichar, but does not name her[230].  The Liber Historiæ Francorum names "Willecharii filiam…Chaldam" as the wife of
2 CONC  Chramn, adding in a later passage that "Willecharius…socer eius" fled with the family to "basilicam sancti Martini"[231].  Gregory of Tours says that Chramn fled to Brittany, where he and his wife and daughters went into hiding w
2 CONC ith "Chanao Count of the Bretons" but were captured and murdered[232].   Chramn & his wife had [two or more] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         daughters (-murdered 560).  Gregory of Tours says that Chramn fled to Brittany, where he and his wife and daughters went into hiding with "Chanao Count of the Bretons" but were captured and murdered[233].   No indicatio
2 CONC n has been found concerning the number or names of Chramn’s daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#ClotaireIdied561B
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chram
