2 CONT Unattributed summary (please identify who you are - it helps if there is a question later - Ben):
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodoric was married once.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a concubine in Moesia, name unknown, and had two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodegotha (ca. 473 – ?). In 494, she was married to Alaric II as a part of her father's alliance with the Visigoths. Ostrogotha or Arevagni (ca. 475 – ?). In 494 or 496, she was married to the king Sigismund of Burgundy as a par
2 CONC t of her father's alliance with the Burgundians. Married to Audofleda in 493 and had one daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT Amalasuntha, Queen of the Goths. She was married to Eutharic and had two children: Athalaric and Matasuentha (the latter being married to Witiges first, then, after Witiges' death, married to Germanus Justinus, neither had childre
2 CONC n). Any hope for a reconciliation between the Goths and the Romans in the person of a Gotho-Roman Emperor from this family lineage was shattered.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death in Ravenna in 526, Theodoric was succeeded by his grandson Athalaric. Athalaric was at first represented by his mother Amalasuntha, who was a regent queen from 526 until 534. The kingdom of the Ostrogoths, however,
2 CONC  began to wane and was conquered by Justinian I starting after the rebellion of 535 and finally ending in 553 with the Battle of Mons Lactarius.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel's summary:
2 CONT
2 CONT Argotta has apparently been identified as Ostrogotha, daughter of Theodoric the Great and an unknown woman from Moesia (present southern Romania). 
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://www.third-millennium-library.com/readinghall/GalleryofHistory/ATTILA/45.html
2 CONT
2 CONT "With these views Alberon married Argotta daughter of Theodemir king of the Goths, formed a strict alliance with the Goths, Vandals, Bohems, and Ostrogoths, and by their aid recovered possession of Arduenna, Lower Alsatia, Brabant
2 CONC ia, Cameracum, and Turnacum, and obtained the title of Rex Cameracensis. His chief residence however was in the Nemus Carbonarium, a part of the forest of Ardennes, where he sacrificed to idols and fortified Mons Hannoniae (Mons i
2 CONC n Hainault), as an asylum against the malice of Meroveus. Argotta bore him Wambert, who married a daughter of the emperor Zeno."
2 CONT
2 CONT (No sources to back this at present, even though it's written well... would advise its use only as guidance for now in the search for sourced information.)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT FMG: Illegitimate daughter of Theodoric "the Great" King of the Goths in Italy & his concubin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gregory of Tours refers to the first wife of Sigismond as the daughter of Theodoric King of Italy, but does not name her [Gregory of Tours III.5, p. 165.].  Iordanes names "unam…Thiudigoto et aliam Ostrogotho" as the two daughters
2 CONC  of Theodoric born "ex concubina…in Moesia" before his marriage to Audofledis, specifying that they came to Italy and were married "unam Alarico Vesegotharum et aliam Sigismundo Burgundzonorum” [Iordanes Getarum, MGH Auct. ant. V.
2 CONC 1, p. 131.].  Her father arranged her marriage as part of his negotiations for an alliance with the Burgundians.  According to Settipani [Settipani (1993), p. 61, footnote 97.], this marriage took place soon after Theoderic arrive
2 CONC d in Italy.  Wolfram suggests [Wolfram (1998), p. 311.] that Theodoric's alliance with the Burgundians was settled in 496.
