1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Julius Nepos (Julije Nepot) (c. 430 - Salona, 9 May 480), The last Roman Emperor===
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julius_Nepos English], [https://hr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julije_Nepot Croatian]
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.enciklopedija.hr/Natuknica.aspx?ID=43425 Nepot, Julije]. Hrvatska enciklopedija, Leksikografski zavod Miroslav Krleža, Zagreb
2 CONT * [https://proleksis.lzmk.hr/38720/ Nepot, Julije], Proleksis enciklopedija (hrv.)
2 CONT * Posavec, V. [http://povijest.net/julije-nepot-posljednji-car-zapadnog-rimskog-carstva/ Julije Nepot - posljednji car Zapadnog Rimskog Carstva], [http://povijest.net/ Hrvatski povijesni portal], 18.2.2008.
2 CONT * '''Bibliography''': [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julius_Nepos#Bibliography En]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nepot je umoren između 25. travnja i 22. lipnja 480. godine (30) u Dioklecijanovoj palači, od ruku svoja dva časnika, Ovide i Vijatora. O načinu na koji je Nepot umoren ne izjašnjava se ni jedan od sačuvanih izvora.(31) Dioklecija
2 CONC nova palača nakon careve smrti ne služi više kao carska palača, jer malo koji car dolazi u nju stanovati, ali je to i dalje carski posjed. Osim Gale Placidije i malog Valentinijana, te Julija Nepota nakon njegova protjerivanja iz 
2 CONC Italije, ni jedan car ili namjesnik nije, koliko je poznato, boravio u palači. Marcelin i Glicerije niti su bili carevi, niti su boravili u palači. Marcelin je zasigurno stolovao u palači namjesnika u Saloni. Ako je Glicerije kao 
2 CONC ex-car i biskup i boravio u palači u vrijeme tzv. druge Nepotove vladavine, nije mu zacijelo tu bila rezidencija. No, palača je svakako imala ulogu ekskluzivnog pribježišta, kako za članove vladarske obitelji tako i za imućne Salo
2 CONC nitance.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nejasno je koji su razlozi naveli Nepotove ubojice Vijatora i Ovidu da se odvaže na takav čin. '''Samo jedan povijesni izvor navodi da je do umorstva došlo na poticaj bivšega cara i salonitanskog biskupa Glicerija, (38) ali, osim 
2 CONC eventualne mržnje ili želje za osvetom, teško je naći ikakav drugi motiv za takav Glicerijev postupak'''.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Read more at''': [http://povijest.net/julije-nepot-posljednji-car-zapadnog-rimskog-carstva/ '''Julije Nepot - posljednji car Zapadnog Rimskog Carstva'''], [http://povijest.net/ Hrvatski povijesni portal]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==About Julius's death:==
2 CONT This below, also applies to the parts of the Croatian article published above.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Cit''' (from Hr wikipedia):
2 CONT
2 CONT "U toku Odoakarovih priprema za bojni pohod u Dalmaciju '''ubio je 9. V. 480. komes Ovida (po imenu sigurno German) svoga vladara Julija Neposa u njegovoj vili kod Salone''' ('''po mišljenju''' [https://www.geni.com/people/don-Fra
2 CONC ne-Buli%C4%87/6000000013194265930 '''don Frane Bulića'''] dogodilo se to u samoj [https://hr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dioklecijanova_pala%C4%8Da Dioklecijanovoj palači].).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes''':
2 CONT # This mentioned above fact by opinion of Mr. don Frane Bulić, seems is not a correct, because at that time, Julius Nepos was in his villa near Salona.
2 CONT # Assassinated was in his villa near Salona or at Diocletian's palace. (?)
2 CONT # Another opinion based at opinion of Mr. don Frane Bulić (don F. Bulić didn't provided a physical proof in his literature), if a Julius was killed in the Diocletian's palace, where is exactly proof for confirmation that.
2 CONT # All Roman soldiers and other persons, who were deserters, spies, opponents of the Emperor or Roman Empire, were executed in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salona#Amphitheatre Amphitheater] in [https://www.geni.com/projects/A
2 CONC ncient-Salona/4479800 Salona], so also [https://www.geni.com/people/Ovida/6000000179090143871 '''Ovida'''] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Viator/6000000179092203822 '''Viator'''], (two his Roman generals) maybe were executed at 
2 CONC the same place, immediately after the Julius's death. (?)
2 CONT # Cit: "Iz činjenice da je Vijator poginuo u borbi, vjerojatno u listopadu 480. godine, a Ovida ili 28. studenoga ili 9. prosinca 482., (41)" - Above article provided a facts that the [https://www.geni.com/people/Viator/6000000179
2 CONC 092203822 '''Viator'''] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Ovida/6000000179090143871 '''Ovida'''] were not executed in Salona. From the above article mentions the fact, that Viator and Ovida died, when and where. The fact that Viato
2 CONC r was killed in battle, probably in October 480, and Ovida on either November 28 or December 9, 482, (41)...' Based on this mentioned fact, '''they were not executed in Salona'''.
