1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anastasius_I_Dicorus
2 CONT
2 CONT Anastasius I Dicorus (Greek: Ἀναστάσιος, translit. Anastásios; c. 431 – 9 July 518) was Eastern Roman emperor from 491 to 518. A career civil servant, he came to the throne at the age of 61 after being chosen by the wife of his pr
2 CONC edecessor, Zeno. His reign was characterised by reforms and improvements in the empire's government, finances, economy and bureaucracy. He is noted for leaving the empire with a stable government, reinvigorated monetary economy an
2 CONC d a sizeable budget surplus, which allowed the empire to pursue more ambitious policies under his successors, most notably Justinian I. Since many of Anastasius' reforms proved long-lasting, his influence over the empire endured f
2 CONC or many centuries.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anastasius was a Miaphysite, and his personal religious tendencies caused tensions throughout his reign in the empire that was becoming increasingly divided along religious lines. He is venerated as a saint by the Syriac Orthodox 
2 CONC Church on 29 July. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *************************************************************
2 CONT In researching heterochromia, I discovered that Aristotle described Anastasius as having the condition just as my mother and I both have it. It's exceptionally rare. I do descend from other Byzantine Emperors, so it's not unusual,
2 CONC  but it is exciting. That's about 1% of the entire population. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anastasius_I_Dicorus
2 CONT
2 CONT Michelle Stein
2 CONT *************************************************************
