2 CONT Page 66:
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.    CHLOTAIRE II, alive 584-628, succeeded as a child to the rule of Neustria, with his headquarters in Paris.  His uncle Siegbert of Austrasin was already dead but his widow Brunhilde, FRèDEGONDE'S sister, kept the feud alive u
2 CONC ntil her own death in 619, when CHLOTAIRE  assumed control of Neustria, acquired Burgundy and became sole ruler of Francia.  In 614 he convoked a council in Paris which promulgated a Magna Carta which increased the powers of the C
2 CONC hurch and the nobility.  The meeting was the most important of the Merovingian epoch.  CHLOTAIRE mar. BERTRUDE who d. 620.
