1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Athalaric (516 – 2 October 534) was the King of the Ostrogoths in Italy between 526 and 534. He was a son of Eutharic and Amalasuntha. His maternal grandfather was Theoderic the Great. He succeeded his grandfather 
2 CONC as king in 526.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT As Athalaric was only ten years old, the regency was assumed by his mother, Amalasuntha. His mother attempted to provide for him an education in the Roman tradition, but the Gothic nobles pressured her to allow them to raise him a
2 CONC s they saw fit. As a result, Athalaric drank heavily and indulged in vicious excesses, which ruined his constitution.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Athalaric]
