1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodegotha '''Theodegotha'''] (5th-century – fl. 502) was a Visigoth queen consort by marriage to king [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alaric_II Alaric II] (494–507).[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodoric_the_Great Theodoric the Great]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her marriage was arranged as an alliance between the Visigoths and the Ostrogoths, though it is disputed when it took place and therefore the exact reasons for the alliance. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the mother of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amalaric Amalaric].
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alaric_II
2 CONT
2 CONT Alaric's heirs were his eldest son, the illegitimate Gesalec, and his younger son, the legitimate Amalaric who was still a child. Gesalec proved incompetent, and in 511 King Theodoric assumed the throne of the kingdom ostensibly o
2 CONC n behalf of Amalaric—Heather uses the word "hijacked" to describe his action. Although Amalaric eventually became king in his own right, the political continuity of the Visigothic kingdom was broken; "Amalaric's succession was the
2 CONC  result of new power structures, not old ones," as Heather describes it. With Amalaric's death in 531, the Visigothic kingdom entered an extended period of unrest which lasted until Leovigild assumed the throne in 568.[13]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel's summary:
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationships:
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT *Father: Theodoric the Great, King of the Ostrogoths (c451 - 526), 
2 CONT *Mother: Unknown Woman from Moesia
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings and half-siblings:
2 CONT *1. Amalasuintha (493 - 535), Queen of Italy (534-535)
2 CONT *3. Ostrogotho/Arevagni (475/480 - before 520), Queen of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT *Alaric I (458 - 507), King of the Visigoths (484 - 507)
2 CONT
2 CONT Child:
2 CONT *Amalric (502 - 531) King of the Visigoths (507-511, 526-531)
