1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Austrigusa''' was a Gepid princess, but her father is unknown. The power struggles among the leading Gepid families make it difficult to speculate about her father. She might have been a daughter of  '''[http://
2 CONC www.geni.com/people/Elemund-King-of-the-Gepids/6000000000722098473 Elemund]''', who ruled the Gepids 535-548. Alternatively, she might have been a sister (or perhaps daughter) of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Thurisind-King-of-th
2 CONC e-Gepids/6000000023305737132 Thurisind]''', who overthrew Elemund's son and ruled 548-circa 560. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Waccho-King-of-the-Lombards/6000000002152926811 Waccho]''' probably married her for political advantage. If so, the date of their marriage (512) might indicate she was the daughter of an earlier rule
2 CONC r. She could have been a granddaughter of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Ardaric-King-of-the-Gepids/6000000007167407935 Ardaric]''' (died circa 460) or a daughter of Trasericus (fl. 505) or of Mundonus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her name, Austrigusa, suggests she might have had a maternal connection to the Ostrogoths.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HUNGARY.htm#OstrogothaMWacho
