1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paulus_(consul_496)_
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Paulus (floruit 496) was a politician of the Eastern Roman Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Paulus was the brother of Anastasius I. His family was Illyrian,[1] and he was the son of Pompeius (born c. 410), a nobleman from Dyrrachium, and Anastasia Constantina (born c. 410), an Arian and a paternal great-granddaughter of 
2 CONC the Roman caesar Constantius Gallus and his wife, Constantina (the daughter of Roman emperor Constantine the Great).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT
2 CONT In 496 he was appointed consul without colleague. He married Magna; they had a daughter, Irene, who married Olybrius, a member of the House of Theodosius.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Croke, Brian (2001). Count Marcellinus and his chronicle. Oxford University Press. p. 89. ISBN 978-0-19-815001-5. Retrieved 12 October 2010. [https://books.google.com/books?id=ep6U-meRt00C&pg=PA89#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks
2 CONC ]
2 CONT *Settipani, Christian, Continuite Gentilice et Continuite Familiale Dans Les Familles Senatoriales Romaines, A L'Epoque Imperiale, Mythe et Realite. Linacre, UK: Prosopographica et Genealogica, 2000. ILL. NYPL ASY (Rome) 03-983
2 CONT * Alan Cameron. Duke University, Greek, Roman and Byzantine Studies The House of Anastasius. Columbia University, pp 259-276. June 1978. Page 270. Accessed 9 April 2020. https://grbs.library.duke.edu/article/viewFile/7451/4919 pag
2 CONC e 17 of PDF. Paul, son of Pompeius.  Married Magna. Children: Irene, Sabianus, Moshianus.
