1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Priest  Ivan (John)==
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.armus.hr/Portals/0/adam/Contents/s5mORmXgQUi54MJNW6tADA/Image/Nadgrobna%20plo%C4%8Da%20sve%C4%87enika%20Ivana.jpg?w=1080&quality=50 Natpis svećenika Ivana], [https://www.armus.hr/izlozbe/stalni-postav/epigraficka-zbir
2 CONC ka Arheološki muzej Split, Salona], Salona, Marusinac, 599. - 603. g.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note''': [https://www.geni.com/people/Marcellinus/6000000017553938484 '''Marcellinus'''] '''was a his brother.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Bio je čuvar bazilike sv. Anastazija na Marusincu u Solinu.
2 CONT * Spominje se [https://www.geni.com/people/Marcelin-of-Dalmatia/6000000179063309832 '''prokonzul Marcelin'''], vjerojatno '''kao namjesnika Dalmacije'''; taj Marcelin je po jednima nećak svećenika Ivana, po drugima njegov sin, a p
2 CONC o trećima brat.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nadgrobna ploča svećenika Ivana sastavljena je od tri ploče. Na početku prvog retka je križ, a na kraju posljednjeg retka hedera (list bršljana). Natpis ima veliko povijesno značenje iz nekoliko razloga. Ponajprije, spominje sveće
2 CONC nika Ivana koji je bio čuvar bazilike sv. Anastazija na Marusincu u Solinu. Nadalje, spominje [https://www.geni.com/people/Marcellinus/6000000017553938484 '''prokonzula Marcelina'''], vjerojatno kao namjesnika Dalmacije; taj Marce
2 CONC lin je po jednima nećak svećenika Ivana, po drugima njegov sin, a po trećima brat. Treće je značenje ovog natpisa u tome što je jedan od najkasnijih salonitanskih i dalmatinskih metričkih natpisa. Još jedna zanimljivost vezana uz 
2 CONC ovaj natpis jest da je [https://www.geni.com/people/Franjo-Buli%C4%87/6000000013194265930 '''don Frani Buliću'''] poslužio kao predložak za njegov nadgrobni natpis.
2 CONT * '''Restitucija''': † Hic iacit(!) Iohannes / peccatur(!) et in/dignus presbiter(!) // †Expleto annorum cir/culo quinto hunc(!) / sibi sepulcrum Io/hannis(!) condere iussit / [https://www.geni.com/people/Marcellinus/6000000017553
2 CONC 938484 '''Marcellino'''] suo procon/sule nato germano prae/sente simul cunctosque(!) // nepotes(!) ornavit tumolum(!) / mente fideli defunctus acces/sit obsis(!) una cum coniuge natis / Anastasii servans reverenda / limina s(an)c(
2 CONC t)i tertio post decimum / Augusti numero mens(is) ind(ictionis).
2 CONT * '''Prijevod''': Ivan, grešnik, tu leži, svećenik nedostojan toga. Godinam ispuniv svojim peti krug dobni za redom grob taj Ivan je dao, narediv, podignut sebi; rođeni brat mu [https://www.geni.com/people/Marcellinus/600000001755
2 CONC 3938484 '''Marcelin'''], prokonzul, nazočan bješe, uz njega, zajedno, bjehu i brojni nećaci svi mu. Umrijevši čistom je vjerom grobu tom ukras sad dao; priključi sad se, ko jamac, skupa sa suprugom, djeci čuvajuć pragove časne Ana
2 CONC staziju svetom. Mjeseca augusta, trinaestog dana po redu, za indikcije druge, vrijeme svog okonča vijeka.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.armus.hr/Portals/0/adam/Contents/s5mORmXgQUi54MJNW6tADA/Image/Nadgrobna%20plo%C4%8Da%20sve%C4%87enika%20Ivana.jpg?w=1080&quality=50|frame|center|300x224px|}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ===English===
2 CONT
2 CONT The tombstone of the priest John is composed of three tablets. At the beginning of the first row is a cross, and at the end of the last row is a header (ivy leaf). The inscription has great historical significance for several reas
2 CONC ons. First of all, he mentions the priest John who was the guardian of the Basilica of St. Anastasia on Marusinac in Solin. Furthermore, he mentions [https://www.geni.com/people/Marcellinus/6000000017553938484 '''Proconsul Marcell
2 CONC inus'''], probably as governor of Dalmatia; this Marcellin is, according to some, the nephew of the priest John, according to others his son, and according to others his brother. The third meaning of this inscription is that it is
2 CONC  one of the latest Salonitan and Dalmatian metric inscriptions. Another interesting thing about this inscription is that [https://www.geni.com/people/Franjo-Buli%C4%87/6000000013194265930 '''don Frani Bulić'''] served as a templat
2 CONC e for his tombstone inscription.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Restitution''': † Hic iacit(!) Iohannes / peccatur(!) et in/dignus presbiter(!) // †Expleto annorum cir/culo quinto hunc(!) / sibi sepulcrum Io/hannis(!) condere iussit / [https://www.geni.com/people/Marcellinus/6000000017553
2 CONC 938484  '''Marcellino'''] suo procon/sule nato germano prae/sente simul cunctosque(!) // nepotes(!) ornavit tumolum(!) / mente fideli defunctus acces/sit obsis(!) una cum coniuge natis / Anastasii servans reverenda / limina s(an)c
2 CONC (t)i tertio post decimum / Augusti numero mens(is) ind(ictionis).<br/>
2 CONT * '''Translation''': John, the sinner, lies there, a priest unworthy of it. For years, having fulfilled the fifth circle of his age in a row, the tomb that John gave, I ordered, was erected for himself; his own brother [https://ww
2 CONC w.geni.com/people/Marcellinus/6000000017553938484 '''Marcelin'''], the proconsul, was present, and with him, together, were his many nephews. Having died by pure faith, he now gave the tomb an ornament; join now, as a guarantor, t
2 CONC ogether with his wife, guarding the thresholds of the holy Anastasia to the children. The month of August, the thirteenth day in a row, for the indications of the second, is the time of the end of its age.
