1 NOTE [FAVthomas.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT    One of the first so-called rois fainéants ("sluggard kings") of theMerovingian dynasty, who held no real power of his own but was ruled bywhoever was his mayor of the palace.
2 CONT    Made king of Austrasia by his father, Dagobert I, in 634, Sigebert wasgoverned first by Bishop Chunibert of Cologne and Duke Adalgisile; then,on Dagobert's death, by Chunibert and Pippin I , the mayor of the palace(d. 640); and
2 CONC  finally by Pippin's son, Grimoald , mayor of the palacefrom 642 or 643 until the king's death.
2 CONT    In the early 640s, when a certain Otto was mayor of the palace,Thuringia succeeded in
2 CONT gaining effective autonomy at Austrasian expense. After Sigebert's death,his young son, Dagobert II, was sent off to an Irish monastery byGrimoald, who briefly established his own son, Childebert (adopted bySigebert when the king 
2 CONC was still childless) on the throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT To cite this page: "Sigebert III" Encyclopædia Britannica
2 CONT <http://www.britannica.com/eb/article?eu=69453&tocid=0&query=sigebert%20iii>
