2 CONT '''Basic Information:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: Unknown. (One user placed his birth at c350 between the Oder and the Vistula in present Western Poland, another suggested Borbetomagus, or present Worms, on the Rhine River. Neither suggestion was backed by a source.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism: Not applicable, he was pagan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Unknown date and location. Could probably be presumed as Borbetomagus or present Worms.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: Borbetomagus, or present Worms, Burgundian Kingdom. He died while defending his capital, as had most of the leadership of the Burgundian kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Unknown. Died in battle, so may not have been buried.
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: King of the Burgundians up to 437, succeeding his brother Giselher (whose death date is not known)
2 CONT
2 CONT Timeline:
2 CONT *c250: Burgundians leave Bornholm in the Baltic Sea and settle in present Pomerania.
2 CONT *369: Emperor Valentinian I pays the Burgundians to attack the Alemanni from their homeland on the Vistula. Shortly after, Fastida, King of the Gepids, attacked from Dacia, driving the Burgundians westward from the Vistula River t
2 CONC o the Rhineland.
2 CONT *375: The Hun Empire defeats the Goths, seizing Scythia (present Ukraine). The Gepids likewise submit to the Huns, indicating that Fastida likely carried out his invasion of the Vistula before this time.
2 CONT *406: The Alans, Suevi, and Vandals cross the Rhine River, invading the Roman Empire with intent to seize all of Gaul. Gjuki, King of the Burgundians, might also have taken part in this invasion.
2 CONT *407: Gjuki, King of the Burgundians, dies, possibly in Borbetomagus (present Worms). He is succeeded by his eldest son, Gundomar.
2 CONT *411: Gundomar dies and is succeeded by his brother Giselher. Gundohar of the Burgundians and Goar, King of the Alans, set up Jovinus as a puppet Emperor of Gaul at Mainz wihtin Germania Secunda.
2 CONT *413: Ataulf and Honorius capture Jovinus at Valentia (present Valence), and the would-be Emperor of Gaul is executed at Narbonne. The Burgundians retain their capital at Borbetomagus (present Worms).
2 CONT *435: Flavius Aetius becomes the protector of Roman Gaul. Among his first tasks is to deal with Burgundian raids into Belgica Secunda.
2 CONT *436: Flavius Aetius pays Hun mercenaries to attack the Burgundian Kingdom on the Rhine River.
2 CONT *437: Borbetomagus (present Worms) falls to Hun mercenaries, and Gundahar dies in the fighting. His death marks the end of the first Kingdom of the Burgundians. Flavius Aeitius moves the Burgundians from the Rhineland to Sapaudia,
2 CONC  the upper Rhone River basin, present Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate Names: Gundahar, Gundicaire, Gunther, Gundahari, Gundaharius, Gundicharius, Gūðhere, Gunnarr, or Gunnar
