2 CONT Page 63:
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.   CLOERIC the Parracide succeeded as King of Cologne.  Soon after the murder he offered CLOVIS the Great a share of SIEGBERT's treasure.  CLOVIS sent officers ostensibly to pick up the gifts, but while CLODERIC was bending over
2 CONC  a chest of gole coins, his head was cleft from behind by a battle axe.  Thus
2 CONT did the great CLOVIS enlarge and secure his kingdom, establishing the Merovingian Dynasty.  CLODERIC mar. a kinswoman of St. CHIOTILDE, Burgundian queen of CLOVIS the Great.  A dau. BLITHILDE mar. ANSBERTUS, Gallo-Roman senator.
2 CONT
