1 NOTE {geni:about_me} There is some confusion around the names and ancestries of Chilperic's two wives. His first wife is said to have been Caratene, daughter of Gundicar and mother of St. Clothilda. His second is said to be a ''sister'
2 CONC ' of Ricimer, not a daughter. Clothilda was the younger of the two daughters, so they must both have been children of Chilperic's first wife Caratene.
2 CONT
2 CONT FMG says: The name of Chilperich´s wife is not known. Gregory of Tours records that Chilperich's wife was drowned by her brother-in-law King Gundobad, after he tied a stone around her neck. The Liber Historiæ Francorum records the
2 CONC  same event.
2 CONT
2 CONT FMG: An epitaph to "Caretenes religiosiæ reginæ", referring to her burial "Lugduni in basilica sancti Michahelis", is included in the compilation of the works of Avitus Bishop of Vienne [Alcimi Ecdicii Aviti Viennensis episcopi Op
2 CONC era quæ superunt, MGH Auct ant VI.2, Epitaphium VI, p. 185.].  It is not clear from the edition consulted whether this epitaph was the bishop's own composition: clearly not all the epitaphs included could have been written by him 
2 CONC as some relate to individuals whose deaths are recorded elsewhere in the second half of the 6th century.  If the epitaph is contemporary with Bishop Avitus, then it presumably refers to the wife of King Gondebaud, to whom Avitus w
2 CONC rote many times, although this is not specified in the text.  It can safely be assumed that she was Catholic.  The text does not reveal any indication of the date of her death, although "506" is added in the margin of the edition 
2 CONC without any indication of the basis.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Cartamene Walia was born about 430 in France. She married 1 Gondobad Gondioc de Bourgogne King of Burgundy about 447 in France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [Notes] 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT    F i Daughter of Gondobad de Bourgogne 
2 CONT
2 CONT    M ii Childeric II de Bourgogne King of Burgundy 
2 CONT
2 CONT    M iii Godogisel de Bourgogne King of Geneva 
