1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anicia Juliana (Constantinople, 462 - 527/528) was a Roman imperial princess, the daughter of the Western Roman Emperor Olybrius, of the Anicii, by Placidia the younger daughter of Emperor Valentinian III and Licin
2 CONC ia Eudoxia.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Flavius Areobindus Dagalaiphus Areobindus, and their children included Olybrius, consul for 491. With her husband, she spent her life at the pre-Justinian court of Constantinople, of which she was considered "both the 
2 CONC most aristocratic and the wealthiest inhabitant".
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anicia_Juliana
