2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%86lffl%C3%A6d_of_Whitby Ælfflæd of Whitby]
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aldfrith_of_Northumbria Aldfrith of Northumbria]
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ealhfl%C3%A6d Ealhflæd, Mercian queen]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Holy relics
2 CONT Oswy and his wife Eanflæd were gifted relics of several saints from Pope Vitalian around 665: Saint Peter, Saint Paul, Saint Laurentius, John the Apostle, Saint Gregory, and Saint Pancras. Eanflæd was also granted "a cross, with a
2 CONC  gold key to it, made out of the most holy chains of the apostles, Peter and Paul". This gift is documented by Bede in Ecclesiastical History of the English People as part of a returning delegation from Rome, which had been led by
2 CONC  Wighard.[52]
