1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''CHIMNECHILDIS [Himnilde/Emnehilde](-676 or >)'''
2 CONT d/o Unknown
2 CONT x SIGEBERT III King of the Franks in Austrasia ([9 Oct 630/19 Jan 631]-1 Feb 656, bur Metz, basilique de Saint-Martin).  
2 CONT *DAGOBERT II King of the Franks in Austrasia.([652/56]-murdered Woëvre forest 23 Dec 679, bur Stenay, basilique Saint-Rémi)
2 CONT *?BILICHILDIS (-murdered forest of Lognes, near Chelles [18 Oct/10 Nov] 675, bur Paris, Saint-Germain-des-Prés) x CHILDERICH II King of the Franks
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Chimnechild of Burgundy''' (7th-century – fl. 662)  (lat. Chimnechildis), ''Himnechichilde, Emnechilde, Imnechilde, Himnilde or Himnehilde'' was a Frankish queen consort of Austrasia of the 8th century, by her marriage to King 
2 CONC Sigebert III.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the mother of 
2 CONT # Bilichild and possibly of 
2 CONT # Dagobert II.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT When Childebert the Adopted died, she opposed the succession of Theuderic III and arranged a marriage between her daughter and Childeric II, whose succession she supported.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family origin 
2 CONT
2 CONT Contemporary documents do not mention its family origin1.
2 CONT
2 CONT The chronicle of Ebersheim, written in the 12th century, specifies that the wife of Duke Adalric Eticho of Alsace, https://www.geni.com/people/Berswinde-d-Austrasie/6000000007331691429 was a niece by her mother of [https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/people/Saint-L%C3%A9ger-bishop-of-Autun/6000000008592674658?through=347217641430012561 Leudegar, (Saint Léger)], bishop of Autun and sister of a queen of the Franks. The marriage between Adalric and Bereswinde having taken p
2 CONC lace at the end of the first half of the 8th century, the Queen of the Franks in question can only be Chimnechilde or < [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bathilde Bathilde] >. The latter cannot correspond, because she was of Servian 
2 CONC origin(?)*, it follows that Chimnechilde is Bereswinde's sister and Saint Léger's niece. However, this chronicle is very late compared to the facts related and is not always taken into account by historians1,2.
2 CONT
2 CONT Onomastic encounters between the Etichonides, from Adalric Eticho and Bereswinde, and the Hugobertides, from the seneschal Hugobert, make Christian Settipani think of a fraternity between Bereswinde and Hugobert. Their father woul
2 CONC d then be the son of a mayor of the Palace of Australasia named Hugh and quoted in 6163. But, he later returns to this fraternity, considering that Hugobert could have other parents. Nevertheless, a cousinage remains possible and 
2 CONC that the mayor of Palais Hugues could be an ancestor of Chimnechilde4.
2 CONT
2 CONT *as translated from French Wikipedia site...Servian is a commune in the Hérault department in the Occitanie region in southern France.
2 CONT
