2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Other names: Baldhild, Bautour, Bauduria, Bat(h)ilde (d'Ascagnie), Bathild, Bathildis, Balthilde, Batilda, Baltilda, Betilda, Bathylle, Badechild, Baldechild, Berthildis, etc. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ David Keys, "Erotic royal seal shows Anglo-French entente", The Independent, 15 June 2003 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Vita Sanctae Bathildis, probably written by a nun of Chelles, and translated and paraphrased in Sainted Women of the Dark Ages pp 264ff. (ref.). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Saint-Claude (Municipality, Jura, France) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Saint Claude 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Joanna Story, Carolingian Connections: Anglo-Saxon England and Carolingian Francia, C. 750-870 (2003) p. 32. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Eddius Stephanus of Ripon, vita of Wilfrid. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Bede reported that Aunemundus, bishop of Lyon, was assassinated at her instigation in 658. 
