2 CONC s nostros Chlodoveus quondam rex" in his deed dated 1 Jun 691, subscribed by "genitricis nostræ Chrodechildis reginæ"[480].  He is named as son of Theoderich in the Cartulaire of Saint-Bertin[481].  The Liber Historiæ Francorum na
2 CONC mes "Chlodoveus filius eius [=Theuderici regis]…puer…ex regina…Chrodchilde" when recording his succession to his father and reign of two years[482].  He succeeded his father in 690 as CLOVIS III King of the Franks, under the autho
2 CONC rity of Pépin d'Herstal [Carolingian], but died after "having reigned four years"[483].  The Chronicon Sancti Medardi Suessionensis records the death in 695 of “Clodoveus puer Rex” and the accession of “Childebertus frater eius”[4
2 CONC 84]. 
