2 CONC am filium suum” in 438, although it is not certain whether he replaced his father entirely as a later passage records that he obtained “Bæticam et Carthaginensem Provincias” on his father´s death in 441[77].  He conquered Mérida i
2 CONC n 439.  He succeeded his father in 441 as RECHILA King of the Suevi in Spain.  He conquered Seville in 441.  Although he was defeated by Roman forces led by Vito in 446, the Romans were unable to prevent the Suevi from continuing 
