1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Arthemia, perhaps a sister of Sacerdos, Gallo-Roman Archbiship of Lyons, 542-559.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: 'Royalty for Commoners', Roderick W. Stuart, 1993, p 128. 'Pedigrees of Some of the Emperor Charlemagne's Descendants', Langston & Buck, 1986, p cv. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthemia
2 CONT
2 CONT Female
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthemia||p30543.htm|Florentinus Bishop of Geneva|d. a 513|p34598.htm|Artemia||p34599.htm|||||||Ruricus Bishop of Limoges||p34600.htm|Hiberia||p34601.htm|
2 CONT
2 CONT      Arthemia was the daughter of Florentinus Bishop of Geneva and Artemia of Lyons.  1 Their daughter, Arthemia, was also known as Artemia of Perthois. Art.2 Arthemia married Munderic Lord of Vitry-en-Perthois, son of Cloderic "t
2 CONC he Parricide" King of Cologne and a kinswoman of St. Clothilde.3,2 Her mother, Artemia was the sister of Saint Sacerdos, the Gallo-Roman Archbishop of Lyons (542-559).3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charts 
2 CONT
