1 OCCU Konge av Kent, Roi de Kent de 725 à 762, King of Kent, Roi de Kent (14e, 746-762), King of Kent 746-762, koning Kent
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bron: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Æthelbert_II_of_Kent
2 CONT
2 CONT Æðelberht II (725 - 762) was king of Kent. Upon the death of his father Wihtred[1], the kingdom was ruled by his three sons, Æðelberht II, Eadberht I and Ælfric. Æthelbert seems to have outlived both of his brothers and later reig
2 CONC ned jointly with his nephew Eardwulf. He died in 762, according to the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle (recorded under 760 due to chronological dislocation). He seems to have left a son, Eadberht II.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Æðelbeorht II, King of Kent1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #150267, d. 748
2 CONT
2 CONT Æðelbeorht II, King of Kent|d. 748|p15027.htm#i150267|Eadric, King of Kent|d. c Aug 686|p15026.htm#i150260||||Ecgbeorht I., King of Kent|d. 4 Jul 673|p15026.htm#i150258||||||||||
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=20 Nov 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT      Æðelbeorht II, King of Kent was the son of Eadric, King of Kent.1 He died in 748.2 He was also reported to have died in 762.3
2 CONT
2 CONT      Æðelbeorht II, King of Kent succeeded to the title of King Æðelbeorht II of Kent in 725.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Æðelbeorht II, King of Kent
