1 OCCU King of the Franks (721-737), comte de Rouergue, Comte d'Autun, Konge av de Chelles 1713-1737 og Frankerne 720-737
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''''Do not confuse him with [http://www.geni.com/people/Thierry-I-comte-d-Autun/6000000002071341413 Thierry I], comte d'Autun'''''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theuderic_IV Théodéric IV]''' was King of the Franks (721-737), as a puppet of [http://www.geni.com/people/Charles-Martel-Duke-of-the-Franks/288390320120001964 Charles Martel], the Mayor of the Pal
2 CONC ace. After his death, the throne was vacant for seven years, until Charles Martel appointed [http://www.geni.com/people/Child%C3%A9ric-III-King-of-the-Franks/6000000003343296649 Childéric III] to succeed him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In some modern literature he is confused with [http://www.geni.com/people/Thierry-I-comte-d-Autun/6000000002071341413 Thierry I d'Autun] (c720-793), who was father of Guilhem de Gellone. See, for example, Michael of Albany and Wal
2 CONC id Amine Salhab, ''The Knights Templar of the Middle East'' (San Francisco, 2006), 52.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theuderic_IV
