1 OCCU Duque de Alsacia, Major Domo, Duke, Hertog van de Alamannen (ca. 640-673/95), Mayor of the Palace, Duc d'Alsace, Maire du Palais du Roy Théodoric III
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Leudesius''' (or Liutheric) was Mayor of the Palace of Neustria (675-676) for Childérich III. He has been called Duke of Alsace, but was not.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is known to have been a son of Erchinoald, Mayor of the Palace of Neustria, and his wife Leutsinde. His paternal grandparents were Leutharius von Schelde and Gerberga Franconia. He had a half-sister named Sigrada (Sigree).
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited his father's properties in 658. In 659 he was involved in a property dispute with the Archdiocese of Rouen and Abbey of Saint-Denis. In 673, the Burgundians under Leodegar defeated Ebroin, the Neustrian mayor, and kin
2 CONC g Theuderic III. They exiled Ebroin to a monastery. The Austrasian mayor Wulfoald took over the power in Neustria, but fled back to Austrasia on the assassination of Childéric II in 675. The Neustrians turned to Leudesius to repla
2 CONC ce him. The next year, Ebroin returned. Leudesius and Theuderic III fled with the royal treasure to Baizieux, where Ebroin overtook them and had Leudesius murdered. [Wikipedia.]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was formerly by some scholars to have been father of Eticho, Duke of Alsace, but modern research suggests Eticho was more probably the son of Dux Adalric.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Of_Alsatia-6
2 CONT
2 CONT =Lendifius Of Alsatia=
2 CONT
