1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==concerns==
2 CONT '''This Sir John resembles https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Richard-de-Lyons-of-Warkworth/6000000002166224010.  Are they supposed to be the same person?  Further research is warranted.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography==
2 CONT Fought Scottish under King Edward I "Longshanks" 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John de Lyonns owned land in Northamptonshire.  Summoned for service against the Scots during the reign of Edward I (circa 1294).  Died circa 1315/6 during the reign of King Edward II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John and Margery Lyons are buried in St. Mary’s Chapel, Warkworth, Northamptonshire.
