1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/AUVERGNE.htm#_Toc55890171
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.        '''GUIGUES [III] de Roche-en-Régnier''' (-before 1320).  Seigneur de Roche-en-Régnier.  “Guigo dominus de Ruppe miles...et Guigo de Ruppe eius filius domicellus, sponsus futurus...Delphinæ filiæ quondam...Bertrandi domin
2 CONC i de Turre militis jan defuncti” guaranteed her dower by charter dated 1298[1611].  He is named in the 2 Jun 1369 charter quoted below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly DAUPHINE de Montboissier, daughter of ---.  Her family origin and marriage is shown in Europäische Stammtafeln[1612].  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly as her first husband, GUYOTTE de Posquières Dame de Bellegarde et de Broussan, daughter of RAYMOND Decan de Posquières Seigneur de Bellegarde et de Brousson [Uzès] & his wife Simone du Caylar (-after 13 Jul 1354).
2 CONC   She married secondly (1320) as his second wife, Robert [I] Seigneur d’Uzès, who became Vicomte d’Uzès in 1328.  Her parentage and two marriages are shown in Europäische Stammtafeln[1613]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Guigues [III] & his first wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT    Guigues [III] & his second wife had two children:
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT
