1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''BEATRIX de Roucy (-7 Nov 1328, bur Angers Cordeliers) dame de Craon'''
2 CONT d/o JEAN [IV] Comte de Roucy Seigneur de Pierrepont & Jeanne de Dreux 
2 CONT x (contract Oct 1312) AMAURY [III] de Craon, s/o MAURICE [V] Seigneur de Craon & Mathilde Berthout van Mechelen ([1280]-26 Jan 1333).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/anjounob.htm#PierreCraondied1376
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfralaoncou.htm#BeatrixRoucyMAmauryCraon
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT JEAN [IV] de Roucy, son of JEAN [III] Comte de Roucy & his wife Isabelle de Mercœur (-before [Jun] 1302, bur Val-le-Roy).  
2 CONT m (before 1292) as her first husband, JEANNE de Dreux, daughter of ROBERT IV Comte de Dreux [Capet] & his wife Beatrix Ctss de Montfort (-11 Apr 1325, bur Saint Dominique near Montargis).
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         '''BEATRIX de Roucy (-7 Nov 1328, bur Angers Cordeliers).  Philippe IV King of France ratified the marriage contract between “Amauri seigneur de Craon” and "Jehan conte de Roucy...damoiselle Béatrix seur dudit comte" by
2 CONC  charter dated Oct 1312[708].  Heiress of la Suze, inherited from her mother[709].  The testament of “Jehanne de Dreux comtesse de Roucy et dame de Puisoye”, dated 1 Oct 1324, bequeathed property to “ma fille de Chastiauvillain [.
2 CONC ..Marie]...ma fille de Craon [...Beatrix]...ma fille de Rouci la Comtesse...ma fille Beatrix fille Jehan mon fil“[710].  A manuscript of the Cordeliers d’Angers lists members of the Craon family buried "dans la chapelle Saint-Jean
2 CONC ", including “Madame Béatrix de Roucy dame de Craon et seconde femme de monsieur Almaury sire de Craon” who died “en l’abit des frères” 7 Nov 1328[711].  m (contract Oct 1312) as his second wife, AMAURY [III] Seigneur de Craon, so
2 CONC n of MAURICE [V] Seigneur de Craon & his wife Mathilde Berthout van Mechelen ([1280]-26 Jan 1333, bur Angers Cordeliers). ''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfralaoncou.htm#BeatrixRoucyMAmauryCraon
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT AMAURY [III] de Craon, son of MAURICE [V] Seigneur de Craon & his wife Mathilde Berthout van Mechelen ([1280]-26 Jan 1333, bur Angers Cordeliers).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m secondly (contract Oct 1312) BEATRIX de Roucy, daughter of JEAN [IV] Comte de Roucy Seigneur de Pierrepont & his wife Jeanne de Dreux (-7 Nov 1328, bur Angers Cordeliers).  Philippe IV King of France ratified the marriage con
2 CONC tract between “Amauri seigneur de Craon” and "Jehan conte de Roucy...damoiselle Béatrix seur dudit comte" by charter dated Oct 1312[337].  Heiress of la Suze, inherited from her mother[338].  The testament of “Jehanne de Dreux com
2 CONC tesse de Roucy et dame de Puisoye”, dated 1 Oct 1324, bequeathed property to “ma fille de Chastiauvillain [...Marie]...ma fille de Craon [...Beatrix]...ma fille de Rouci la Comtesse...ma fille Beatrix fille Jehan mon fil“[339].  A
2 CONC  manuscript of the Cordeliers d’Angers lists members of the Craon family buried "dans la chapelle Saint-Jean", including “Madame Béatrix de Roucy dame de Craon et seconde femme de monsieur Almaury sire de Craon” who died “en l’abi
2 CONC t des frères” 7 Nov 1328[340].''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Amaury [III] & his second wife had nine children
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/anjounob.htm#PierreCraondied1376
2 CONT ----
