1 NAME Bernard /de la Tour/
2 GIVN Bernard
2 _MARNM de la Tour
1 NAME Bernard III, seigneur de la Tour
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1275
2 PLAC France
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 DEC 1325
1 OCCU seigneur de la Tour
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/AUVERGNE.htm#BernardIIITourdied1325
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         BERNARD (-19 Dec 1325).  The testament of "dominus Bertrandus dominus de Turre filius quondam…Bernardi domini de Turre militis", dated 1285, appoints "Bernardum filium suum" as his heir[1771].  Seigneur de la Tour.  "Be
2 CONC rnardus dominus de Turre et Bertrandus de Turre eius frater" divided their inheritance, in the presence of "domina Beatrice de Olierguio domina de Turre", by charter dated Jul 1304[1772].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (contract 1292, confirmed 17 Nov 1295) BEATRIX de Rodez, daughter of HENRI [II] Comte de Rodez & his second wife Mascarose de Comminges (-Apr 1315).  A manuscript of Rodez convent names "tres filias…Belburgem, Beatricem et
2 CONC  Cæciliam" as thr children of "Henricus comes Ruthenensis filius Hugonis" and his second wife "domina Mascarosa de Convenis", adding that Beatrix married "nobili Bernardo de Turre" with a dowry of "baroniæ d’Escorales et sancti Cr
2 CONC istofori"[1773].  The marriage contract between "Henrico…comite Ruthenensi…Beatricem filiam" and "Beatrice domina de Turre relicta domini Bernardi de Turre militis defuncti…filium…Bernardum" is dated 1292[1774].  The marriage cont
2 CONC ract between "Bernardus de Turre domicellus filius et heres…quondam domini Bertrandi domini de Turre militis patris mei jam defuncti…" and "domino Henrico…comite Ruthenensi…Beatrici filiæ" was confirmed 17 Nov 1295[1775].  The tes
2 CONC tament of "Henricus…comes Ruthenensis", dated 1301, appoints "filiam suam Beatricem…ex matrimonio…dominæ Mascarosæ de Convenis…natam uxorem…Bernardi de Torre" as his heir "in…baronia sua d’Escoralha et sancti Cristofori"[1776].  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Bernard & his wife had five children: 
