2 NICK Aymeri
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1255
2 ADDR
3 CITY Rochechouart
3 STAE Aquitaine-Limousin-Poitou-Charentes
3 CTRY France
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1297
1 OCCU Baron de la Rochefoucauld, seigneur du Marthon et du Monteil, Consanguinité 0.2%
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ANGOULEME.htm#GuyVIRochefoucaulddied1295B '''From Medlands:''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''AIMERY [II] de la Rochefoucauld''' (-1297 or after).  “...Guy et Aimery de la Roche frères...” witnessed the charter dated 2 Feb 1272 which confirmed the emancipation by “Aimery vicomte de Rochechouart” of “Marguerite sa fille”
2 CONC  and his grant to her “en faveur de son mariage avec Arnaud Bochart damoiseau...rente...sur les biens de feue dame Jeanne sa femme mère de la dite Marguerite”[1268].  Seigneur de la Rochefoucauld.  His testament is dated 1297[1269
2 CONC ]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (before Mar 1285) as her second husband, DAUPHINE de la Tour, widow of RAYNAUD d’Aubusson Seigneur de la Borne et du Monteil-au-vicomte, daughter of BERNARD [III] Seigneur de la Tour & his wife Yolande --- (-1299 or after).  "Ay
2 CONC mericus de Rupe domicellus et Delphina eius uxor" acknowledged that "Raynaldo d’Albusso quondam marito eiusdem Delphinæ" had received the dowry for his marriage and "Bertrandus dominus de Turre miles frater dictæ Delphinæ…" increa
2 CONC sed the dowry by charter dated end-Mar 1285[1270].  The testament of "Dalphina de Turre relicta quondam Aymerici de Rupe domini eiusdem loci", dated 1299, appoints "Guidonem filium meum primogenitum" as her heir, divides her remai
2 CONC ning property between "alios liberos meos…Gaufridus filius meus…Agnes filia mea primogenita…Aymericus filius meus…Margarita filia mea", and appoints "dominam Beatricem d’Olyergue dominam de Turre…" among her executors[1271]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Aimery [II] & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         GUY [VII] de la Rochefoucauld (-1344 or after).  The testament of "Dalphina de Turre relicta quondam Aymerici de Rupe domini eiusdem loci", dated 1299, appoints "Guidonem filium meum primogenitum" as her heir[1272].  Se
2 CONC igneur de la Rochefoucauld.  His testament is dated 1344[1273].  -        SEIGNEURS de la ROCHEFOUCAULD[1274]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         GEOFFROY de la Rochefoucauld (-before 1329).  The testament of "Dalphina de Turre relicta quondam Aymerici de Rupe domini eiusdem loci", dated 1299, divides her remaining property between "alios liberos meos…Gaufridus f
2 CONC ilius meus…Agnes filia mea primogenita…Aymericus filius meus…Margarita filia mea"[1275].  Seigneur de Verteuil.  -        SEIGNEURS de VERTEUIL[1276]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         AGNES de la Rochefoucauld .  The testament of "Dalphina de Turre relicta quondam Aymerici de Rupe domini eiusdem loci", dated 1299, divides her remaining property between "alios liberos meos…Gaufridus filius meus…Agnes 
2 CONC filia mea primogenita…Aymericus filius meus…Margarita filia mea"[1277].  m HUGUES Seigneur de Confolens et de Chabanais, son of ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         AIMERY de la Rochefoucauld (-1362 or alter).  The testament of "Dalphina de Turre relicta quondam Aymerici de Rupe domini eiusdem loci", dated 1299, divides her remaining property between "alios liberos meos…Gaufridus f
2 CONC ilius meus…Agnes filia mea primogenita…Aymericus filius meus…Margarita filia mea"[1278].  Seigneur de la Boissière.  m CHARLOTTE de Jaunay, daughter of CHARLES de Jaunay Seigneur d’Ausance & his wife Philippa de la Haye.  Aimery &
2 CONC  his wife had one child:  i)          GUY de la Rochefoucauld (-[1400]).  Seigneur de la Boissière.  m ---.  The name of Guy’s wife is not known.  Guy & his wife had one child:  (a)       FOULQUES de la Rochefoucauld (-after 1406)
2 CONC .  Seigneur de la Boissière. 
2 CONT
2 CONT e)         MARGUERITE de la Rochefoucauld .  The testament of "Dalphina de Turre relicta quondam Aymerici de Rupe domini eiusdem loci", dated 1299, divides her remaining property between "alios liberos meos…Gaufridus filius meus…A
2 CONC gnes filia mea primogenita…Aymericus filius meus…Margarita filia mea"[1279]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ANGOULEME.htm#GuyVIRochefoucaulddied1295B '''From Medlands:''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''AYMAR de la Rochefoucauld''' (-after 1300).  Seigneur de Cellefroin.  Doyen of the church of Bordeaux after 1300. 
