1 NAME Béatrix /De Rodez/ dame de Scorailles and Saint-Christophe
2 GIVN Béatrix
2 SURN De Rodez
2 NSFX dame de Scorailles and Saint-Christophe
2 _MARNM de la Tour
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1275
2 PLAC France
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1309
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Comtesse de Rodez, Viscomtesse de Creyssels, Mascaronne de Comminges 
2 CONT
2 CONT lady of Scorailles, Saint-Christophe;
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/toulnoreast.htm#BeatriceRodezMBernardIIILaTour
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         BEATRIX de Rodez (-Apr 1315).  A manuscript of Rodez convent names "tres filias…Belburgem, Beatricem et Cæciliam" as thr children of "Henricus comes Ruthenensis filius Hugonis" and his second wife "domina Mascarosa de C
2 CONC onvenis", adding that Beatrix married "nobili Bernardo de Turre" with a dowry of "baroniæ d’Escorales et sancti Cristofori"[1065].  The testament of "Mascarona…comitissa Ruthenensis", made Mar 1291, makes bequests to "…filiabus no
2 CONC stris…Valborges, Cæciliæ et Beatrici"[1066].  The marriage contract between "Henrico…comite Ruthenensi…Beatricem filiam" and "Beatrice domina de Turre relicta domini Bernardi de Turre militis defuncti…filium…Bernardum" is dated 12
2 CONC 92[1067].  The marriage contract between "Bernardus de Turre domicellus filius et heres…quondam domini Bertrandi domini de Turre militis patris mei jam defuncti…" and "domino Henrico…comite Ruthenensi…Beatrici filiæ" was confirmed
2 CONC  17 Nov 1295[1068].  The testament of "Henricus…comes Ruthenensis", dated 1301, appoints "filiam suam Beatricem…ex matrimonio…dominæ Mascarosæ de Convenis…natam uxorem…Bernardi de Torre" as his heir "in…baronia sua d’Escoralha et 
2 CONC sancti Cristofori"[1069].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (contract 1292, 17 Nov 1295) BERNARD Seigneur de la Tour, son of BERTRAND [V] Seigneur de la Tour {Puy-de-Dôme} & his wife Beatrix d’Olliergues (-19 Dec 1325). 
2 CONT * Reference: [https://gw.geneanet.org/chatelaine87?lang=en&pz=clara&nz=adobati&p=beatrix&n=de+rodez Geneanet Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 29 2024, 9:54:43 UTC''
