2 CONT
2 CONT a)        ''' ISOARDE d’Agoult''' ([1255/57?]-before 1281).  Courcelles records her parentage and marriage “en 1272”[285].  He cites no source, but the marriage is indicated by the 6 May 1299 charter which names her husband, cited
2 CONC  above under her father.  It is also suggested by the use of the name “Amiel” for one of her sons.  Pollastri records that Charles I King of Sicily [Anjou-Capet] arranged her first proposed marriage[286].  Her subsequent marriage 
2 CONC with Bertrand de Baux confirms that this earlier marriage did not proceed.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed''' ([1269/70], contract terminated) to TOMMASO di Sanseverino, son of RUGGIERO Conte di Sanseverino, Conte di Marsico & his second wife Teodora d’Aquino (-after 1317).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [1272] )  as his first wife, BERTRAND [III] de Baux Seigneur de Courthezon, son of RAYMOND [II] de Baux co-Prince d’Orange & his [first/second wife [Bigne ---]/Laure Adhémar] (-1305). 
