1 NAME Jean /de Craon/ Seigneur de Dommart, de Bernarville, de Clacy
2 GIVN Jean
2 NSFX Seigneur de Dommart, de Bernarville, de Clacy
2 _MARNM de Craon
1 NAME /de Craon/
2 GIVN
2 SURN de Craon
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1346
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 1400
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''JEAN de Craon (-<1400).  Seigneur de Dommart, de Bernarville, de Clacy, de Montsoreau et de Nouâtre.  Vidame de Laon, de iure uxoris'''
2 CONT s/o GUILLAUME de Craon & MARGUERITE de Flandre
2 CONT x (1364) MARIE de Châtillon Vidamesse de Laon
2 CONT >>i)          SIMON de Craon (killed in battle Agincourt 25 Oct 1415)
2 CONT >>ii)         JEAN de Craon (-1420)
2 CONT >>iii)        MARGUERITE de Craon 
2 CONT >>iv)        MARIE de Craon
2 CONT >>v)         JACQUELINE de Craon 
2 CONT >>vi)        other children .  
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/anjounob.htm#GuillaumeCraondied1387
2 CONT ----
2 CONT GUILLAUME de Craon (after 15 Apr 1318-8 Jun 1387, bur Châteaudun, Abbaye des Cordeliers). m (before 4 May 1341) MARGUERITE de Flandre, daughter of JEAN de Flandre Seigneur de Dendermonde et de Nesle-en-Picardie & his wife Beatrix 
2 CONC de Châtillon (-after 3 Jul 1387) Guillaume & his wife had children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >c) '''JEAN de Craon (-before 1400).  Seigneur de Dommart, de Bernarville, de Clacy, de Montsoreau et de Nouâtre.  Vidame de Laon, de iure uxoris.  “Pierre de la Ferté-Bernard, Jeanne de Châtillon, Jean de Craon vidame de Laonnais
2 CONC  et Marie sa femme” and “Robert et Jean de Béthune” reached agreement about “l’héritage de Coucy” by charter dated 8 Jul 1389[403].  m (1364) MARIE de Châtillon Vidamesse de Laon, daughter of GAUCHER de Châtillon Seigneur de Rozoy
2 CONC  et de Clacy, Vidame de Laon & his wife Marie de Coucy (-1410).  Duchesne records her parentage and marriage[404].  “Pierre de la Ferté-Bernard, Jeanne de Châtillon, Jean de Craon vidame de Laonnais et Marie sa femme” and “Robert 
2 CONC et Jean de Béthune” reached agreement about “l’héritage de Coucy” by charter dated 8 Jul 1389[405].  Duchesne records her death in 1410[406].  Jean & his wife had children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>i)          SIMON de Craon (killed in battle Agincourt 25 Oct 1415).  Duchesne records his parentage and death at Agincourt[407].  Seigneur de Dommart et de Clacy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>ii)         JEAN de Craon (-1420).  Duchesne records his parentage, capture at Agincourt, and death “peu après”[408].  Seigneur de Dommart.  m GUYOTTE de Lonroy, daughter of JEAN Seigneur de Lonroy & his wife Marie de Quérieu Da
2 CONC me de Monsures.  Jean & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>iii)        MARGUERITE de Craon .  Duchesne records her parentage and two marriages[413].  Dame de Tour-sur-Marne.  m firstly (10 May 1381) BERNARD de Dormans Seigneur de Soupy, son of ---.  m secondly JEAN de Croÿ Seigneur de C
2 CONC roÿ et de Renty, son of --- (-killed in battle Agincourt 25 Oct 1415, bur Saint-Bertin). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>iv)        MARIE de Craon .  m GAUCHER de Thourotte Seigneur d’Aillebaudières, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>v)         JACQUELINE de Craon .  m JAN van Gisel Heer van Dudzele, son of ROGER van Gistel & his wife Elisabeth [Margareta] van Dudzele.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>vi)        other children .  Duchesne records that Jean de Craon and his wife had 18 children, of whom 5 died young[414]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/anjounob.htm#GuillaumeCraondied1387
2 CONT ----
