1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margherita_di_Savoia_(1295-1339)_
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAVOY.htm#Margueritedied1339
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.         MARGUERITE de Savoie (-1339).  The testament of "Sibilla comitissa Sabaudiæ, dominaque Baugiaci, uxor…domini Amedei comitis Sabaudiæ" dated 1294 grants bequests to "…filiæ nostræ Elyonori, Guillermo comiti Altissiodoren
2 CONC si eius marito…filiæ nostræ Margaretæ…filiæ nostræ Agneti…filio nostro Aymoni…filium nostrum Eduardum…in pupillari ætate…illum quem gestamus in utero"[575].  "Margarita di Savoia" made a donation to "Conte Amedeo suo Padre" of a s
2 CONC um on money bequeathed to her under the last testament of "Dama Sibilla sua Madre" dated 6 Jan 1296[576], presumably as part of the arrangements for her forthcoming marriage.  The Chronicon Astense records the marriage in 1296 of 
2 CONC "Johannes…Marchio Montisferrati" and "Amadeum Sabaudiæ comitem…Margaritam eius filiam" who had previously been betrothed to "Johanni filio Humberti Delfini"[577].  The contract of marriage between "Gioanni Marchese di Monferrato" 
2 CONC and "Margarita di Savoia figlia del Conte Amedeo V di Savoia" is dated 23 Mar 1296[578].  A contract dated 14 Mar 1305 between "Marchese Manfredo di Saluzzo" as Governor of the Marquisate of Monferrato and "Margarita di Savoia fig
2 CONC lia del Conte Amedeo Vedova del suddetto Marchese" confirmed her possession of the castles of Lanzo, Ciriè and Caselle as part of her dowry[579].  The testament of "Conte Amedeo di Savoia" dated 27 Sep 1307 names "…Eleonora, Marga
2 CONC rita, ed Agnes sue figlie"[580].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed''' (contract broken before 1296) to JEAN de la Tour du Pin et de Coligny, son of HUMBERT de la Tour du Pin et de Coligny, Dauphin de Viennois & his wife Anne Dauphine de Viennois [Bourgogne-Capet] (before [1277]-Pont 
2 CONC de Sorgues, Avignon 4 Mar 1319, bur Grenoble église Saint-André).  He succeeded his father in 1307 as JEAN [II] Dauphin de Viennois, Comte d'Albon.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (contract 23 Mar 1296) GIOVANNI I Marchese di Monferrato, son of GUGLIELMO VI Marchese di Monferrato & his third wife Infanta doña Beatriz de Castilla (Milan 1278-[9] Mar 1305). 
