2 CONT '''Nobility, Military figure. He succeeded his father as Duke of Bourbon and Seigneur de Mercœur in 1410. After the murder of Louis de Orleans he changed sides and joined the Armagnacs with whom he entered Paris in 1413. He succes
2 CONC sfully fought the english in the Limousin and in Guyenne. Although he survived Battle of Azincourt in 1415, he was captured by the english and spent the rest of his life in prison in London. His body was brought to Souvigny and bu
2 CONC ried in the old chapel of the Seigneurs de Bourbon. In 1410 he married Marie de Berry, Duchess of Auvergne who bore him three children. He also had five illegitimate children''' including Jean, Bishop of Puy and Abbott of Cluny an
2 CONC d Marguerite who married Rodrigo de Villandrando.
