1 NOTE Amadeus VI or Amadeo of Savoy had joined the force of Louis I Count of Anjou to take Naples from Charles Duke of  Durazzo.  An epidemic hit the army of France, and one of it's victims was Amadeo of Savoy, age 49.  March 1 1383.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amadeus VI Count of Savoy reigned from the death of his father, Amadeus V in 1343 to his own death in 1383.
