2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p14/9d/9f/30/40/53444869007a3b61/59fea1c9-e457-4c16-b8ef-693ff8fb0f16_original.jpg?hash=bcd374ec8463746e15a49402b7f31c190c7f87cf7e6f42d01401f7e9ad264441.1793865599
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL (of) Fleet From Roquevaire
2 _PRIM Y
2 NOTE The Roquevaire Fleet is registered with the Armorial of Hozier of 1696, with three of its members: N. de Flotte judge of Roquevaire, Jean-Baptiste and Jean-Augustin de Flotte, bourgeois. The first is François Flotte, the second hi
3 CONC s brother and the third his uncle. They carry the same weapons: azure with three gold auriols surmounted by a lambel of gueules (or with three pendants of gueules, according to Robert de Briançon, which is an implicit precision). 
3 CONC These are the arms of the former lords of Auriol, with a break. The loriot or auriol in Provençal (auriòu) also appears in the coat of arms of the city of Auriol.
3 CONT
3 CONT Later, in order to highlight their extraction, the Roquevaire Fleet will take up the primitive weapons of their family, in a quartered: at 1 and 4, of azure with three gold loriots surmounted by a silver lambel (Auriol), at 2 and 
3 CONC 3 rhombuses of gules and silver with gold head (Flotte).
