1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from MEDLANDS 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         JEAN de Vienne .  The testament of “Jehanne de Saincte Croix dame de Montrunt et de Chastel Maillet”, dated 8 Oct 1363 published early Dec 1363, bequeathed property to “Vauthier et Jehan de Vyanne freres, enffanz de mo
2 CONC n seigneur et marit...Henry de Vyanne sires de Mirebel”[550].  Seigneur de Montrond.  Père Anselme records his parentage and that he died childless, without citing the corresponding primary source[551].  His parentage and his fath
2 CONC erhood of at least one child are confirmed by the testament of his brother Gauthier.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Jean’s wife is not known.  Jean & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1)       '''GAUTHIER de Vienne ([1378]-killed in battle Nikopolis 1396).  The testament of “Gauthier de Vienne [seigneur de Mirebel]”, dated “Feb 1399 (O.S.)” [date should be 1390?], named as his heir “Gauthier de Vienne fils de 
2 CONC feu Jean de Vienne son frère” with “[les] enfants de Jeanne sa sœur dame de Saint-Dizier...Jean de Vienne sire de Roulans, Jean de Vienne sire de Pagny et Henri son frère” as successive substitutes[552].  A monument at Nikopolis r
2 CONC ecords the deaths there of “...Vauthier de Vienne sire de Mirebel 1378-1396...”[553].  m as her first husband, ISABELLE d’Estouteville, daughter of ROBERT [VII] Seigneur d’Estouteville & his wife Marguerite de Montmorency (-after 
2 CONC 28 Oct 1438).  She married secondly (contract 8 Nov 1401) Jean de Béthune Seigneur de Locres et de Mareuil.  She married thirdly (after 1415) as his second wife, Henri [III] Seigneur de Hans.  The primary sources which confirm her
2 CONC  parentage and three marriages have not been identified.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Battle of Nicopolis https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Nicopolis
