1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from MEDLANDS 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''HENRI [III] de Hans, son of HENRI [II] Seigneur de Hans & his wife Beatrix de Commercy (-after 1436).  Barthélemy records his parentage[1045].  Seigneur de Hans.  Henri swore allegiance “pour St-Germainmont et Hanongne, du chef
2 CONC  de Marie de Lor sa femme” by charter dated 2 Feb 1392[1046].  He is noted as living in his son’s 21 May 1436 charter cited below.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ([1380/90]) MARIE de Lor, daughter of GAUTHIER de Lor Seigneur de Brais & his wife Marguerite de Walcourt ([1365/70]-[2 Feb 1392/1415], bur Foigny).  Henri swore allegiance “pour St-Germainmont et Hanongne, du chef de Ma
2 CONC rie de Lor sa femme” by charter dated 2 Feb 1392[1047].  Barthélemy records that she was buried with her supposed daughter Agnès (see below). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m secondly (after 1415) as her third husband, ISABELLE d’Estouteville, widow firstly of GAUTHIER de Vienne Seigneur de Mirebel and secondly of JEAN de Béthune Seigneur de Locres et de Mareuil, daughter of ROBERT [VII] Seigneur 
2 CONC d’Estouteville & his wife Marguerite de Montmorency (-after 28 Oct 1438).''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri [III] & his first wife had [two] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         [AGNES de Hans ([1381/91]-[30 May 1393, bur Foigny]).  Barthélemy records Agnes as daughter of Henri [III] Seigneur de Hans by his first wife Marie de Lor, notes that she married Thomas de Coucy Seigneur de Vervins, tha
2 CONC t she died 30 May 1393, and was buried at Foigny “auprès de sa mère”[1048].  He cites no sources on which he bases this information.  The chronology is wrong.  Assuming that Henri [III] did have a daughter named Agnes, and that sh
2 CONC e died 30 May 1393, her date of birth (estimated from her mother’s birthdate) suggests that she would probably have died unmarried or recently married.  If that is correct, Agnes, wife of Thomas de Coucy, would have been the daugh
2 CONC ter of an earlier Seigneur de Hans (see above).] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         JACQUES [III] de Hans (-[5 Sep 1465/26 Jun 1478]).  The date of the following charter indicates that Jacques was born from his father’s first marriage.  His date of death suggests that he would have been younger than hi
2 CONC s supposed sister Agnes.  The king granted “[les] chasteaus, terre, seigneurie et revenus de Bruieres lés Montoiz” to “Iaques de Hans chevalier” by charter dated 7 Apr 1423[1049].  Jacques de Hans “chevalier, comme procureur de so
2 CONC n père” swore allegiance for “St-Jean-sur-Toube, Cornay, Haulzy, St-Pierremont et Thénorgues” by charter dated 21 May 1436[1050].  Seigneur de Hans.  m ISABELLE de Béthune, daughter of JEAN de Béthune Seigneur de Locres et de Mare
2 CONC uil & his wife Isabelle d’Estouteville (-[before 28] Aug [after Aug 1480], bur Ecry Saint-Didier).  “Robert de Bethune chevalier seigneur de Marueil en Brie, d’Hostel et de Baye” and “madame Isabel de Bethune sa seur femme...de...
2 CONC Iacques seigneur de Hans et des Armoises chevalier” agreed the succession of “monseigneur Iehan de Bethune chevalier iadis seigneur desdits lieux...et madame Isabel d’Estouteville leurs pere et mere”, noting property inherited fro
2 CONC m “feuë madame Marguerite de Montmorency dame d’Estouteville” by “ladite madame Isabel d’Estouteville sa fille...”, by charter dated 29 May 1441[1051].  An epitaph at Ecry Saint-Didier records the burial of “Isabel de Bethune dame
2 CONC  de Hans, des Armoises et d’Escry” 28 Aug 1453 [year incorrect][1052].  She is named in her son’s Aug 1480 charter, quoted below, in which he acted as her proxy.  Jacques [III] & his wife had [two or more] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         HENRI [IV] de Hans (-[Aug 1480/27 Aug 1484]).  Seigneur de Hans.  “Henry de Hans chevalier seigneur dudit Hans et d’Escry”, as heir and proxy of “madame Ysabel de Bethune veufue de monseigneur Iacques de Hans en son viv
2 CONC ant chevalier seigneur de Hans et des Armoises, dame douagere dudit Hans et des Armoises sa mère”, sold property “deux fiefs...le Fief de Locres mouvant de la Comté de Soissons...”, which she had inherited “par la mort...de feu so
2 CONC n...pere monseigneur Iehan de Bethune dit de Locres en son vivant chevalier seigneur de Mareul, d’Hostel et de Baye”, to “messire Guillaume de Biche chevalier, President des Finances, Conseiller et Chambellan du Roy...”, by charte
2 CONC r dated Aug 1480[1053].  He presumably died before 27 Aug 1484, the date of his son’s charter cited below.  m [JACQUELINE/LOUISE] van Gistel, daughter of ---.  Barthélemy names “Jacqueline ou plutôt Louise de Guistelles” as the wi
2 CONC fe of Henri [IV] de Hans, without citing the sources which confirm the information[1054].  Mistress (1): ---.  The name of Henri’s mistress is not known.  Henri [IV] & his wife had children:  i)          JACQUES [IV] de Hans (-[18
2 CONC  Mar 1516/Dec 1519]).  Seigneur de Hans.  Jacques swore homage for “Haulzy, de la baronnie de Saint-Jean-sur-Tourbe...” by charter dated 27 Aug 1484[1055].  Baron d’Arzillières, de iure uxoris.  The Chronicle of Saint-Martin de Hu
2 CONC iron records that King Louis XII granted the right to hold two fairs at Huiron “à la demande de Jacques de Grandpré chevalier seigneur de Hans, baron d’Arzillières et de Louise de Hangest sa femme” dated Feb 1506[1056].  Comte de 
2 CONC Dampierre: “Claude d’Espeuse chevalier” swore allegiance to “Jacques de Grandpré chevalier seigneur de Hans, comte de Dampierre, baron d’Arzillières” for “la terre d’Epense” by charter dated 22 Apr 1511[1057].  The Chronicle of Sa
2 CONC int-Martin de Huiron records an agreement between “Jacques de Grandpré et Louise de Hangest sa femme” and the abbot of Huiron regarding rights in the woods at Huiron, dated 18 Mar 1516[1058].  He was presumably deceased in Dec 151
2 CONC 9, the date of his son’s charter cited below.  m (1504) LOUISE de Hangest, daughter of GUILLAUME de Hangest Baron d’Arzillières, de Dampierre-en-Astenois, de Blaise, d’Hauteville et de Landricourt & his wife Marguerite de Torcenai
2 CONC .  Barthélemy records her parentage and marriage, without citing the sources which confirm the information[1059].  The Chronicle of Saint-Martin de Huiron records that King Louis XII granted the right to hold two fairs at Huiron “
2 CONC à la demande de Jacques de Grandpré chevalier seigneur de Hans, baron d’Arzillières et de Louise de Hangest sa femme” dated Feb 1506[1060].  The Chronicle of Saint-Martin de Huiron records an agreement between “Jacques de Grandpré
2 CONC  et Louise de Hangest sa femme” and the abbot of Huiron regarding rights in the woods at Huiron, dated 18 Mar 1516[1061].  Jacques [IV] & his wife had two children:  (a)       GUILLAUME de Hans (-[1526]).  Barthélemy records his p
2 CONC arentage, without citing the sources which confirm the information[1062].  Seigneur de Hans.  Guillaume de Grandpré swore homage for “Hauzy, Melzicourt, Saint-Jean-sur-Tourbe...” by charter dated Dec 1519[1063].  Barthélemy record
2 CONC s that Guillaume died “vers 1586, date à laquelle son beau-frère Henri de Linange rachetait la baronnie d’Arzillières”[1064].  The year must be incorrect: presumably Guillaume died [1526].  (b)       MADELEINE de Hans (-after 1544
2 CONC ).  Barthélemy records her parentage and two marriages, noting that she succeeded her brother and that her only daughter by her first marriage “Anne de Linange...apporta la seigneurie de Hans à son époux Claude de Bossut seigneur 
2 CONC de Longueval”, without citing the sources which confirm the information[1065].  m firstly HEINRICH [Hesso] Graf von Leiningen, son of EMICH Graf von Leiningen-Dagsburg und Hartenburg Seigneur d’Apremont & his wife Anna von Elter h
2 CONC eiress of Apremont (before 1530).  m secondly (after 1532) FRANÇOIS de Cadenet, son of ---.  ii)         MARIE de Hans (-before 1488).  Barthélemy records her parentage and marriage, without citing the sources which confirm the in
2 CONC formation[1066].  m as his first wife, RAOUL de Coucy Seigneur de Vervins, son of --- (-Chémery 1515, bur Vervins).  Chambellan du roi.  Henri [IV] had one illegitimate child by Mistress (1):  iii)        JACQUES bâtard de Hans (-
2 CONC after 10 Jul 1478).  A charter dated 10 Jul 1478 records that “madame Ysabel de Bethune vefue de feu...Iaques en son vivant seigneur de Hans et des Armoises” donated property to “Iaques bastard de Hans filz illegitime de...Henry s
2 CONC eigneur de Hans, qui est filz aisné dudit feu...Iaques seigneur de Hans et de ladite dame Ysabel” by charter dated 10 Jul 1478[1067].  b)         [two or more] sons (-after 10 Jul 1478).  Their existence is confirmed by the 10 Jul
2 CONC  1478 charter of their mother in which she names their brother Henri [IV] as “filz aisné dudit feu...Iaques seigneur de Hans et de ladite dame Ysabel”. 
