2 CONT 2. JEAN de Vendôme (-after 1460).  Vidame de Chartres.  '''m as her second husband, CATHERINE de Thouars Dame de Pouzauges, de Chabanais et de Conflant, widow of GILLES de Laval Seigneur de Rays, daughter of MILON [II] de Thouars 
2 CONC Seigneur de Pouzauges & his wife --- (-2 Dec 1462).  Père Anselme records her parentage and two marriages without citing the corresponding primary sources[337].  The record of the 1503 hearing relating to the dispute over the inhe
2 CONC ritance of the county of Bigorre records that "autre messire Miles de Toars", son of "messire Regnaud de Toars" and his wife, married "Béatrix de Montéjon", by whom he had "Catherine de Thoars" who married "Jehan de Vendosme" and 
2 CONC were parents of "messire Jehan de Vendosme père…du monsieur Jacques de Vendôsme demandeur"[338].  Jean & his wife had two children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         JEAN de Vendôme (-after 24 Feb 1481).  The record of the 1503 hearing relating to the dispute over the inheritance of the county of Bigorre records that "autre messire Miles de Toars", son of "messire Regnaud de Toars" 
2 CONC and his wife, married "Béatrix de Montéjon", by whom he had "Catherine de Thoars" who married "Jehan de Vendosme" and were parents of "messire Jehan de Vendosme père…du monsieur Jacques de Vendôsme demandeur"[339].  Vidame de Char
2 CONC tres.  Seigneur de Pouzauges.  Prince de Chabanais.  m JEANNE de Brezé, daughter of PIERRE [II] de Brezé Baron de Maulevrier & his wife Jeanne Crespin (-after 1465).  Jean & his wife had one child
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         JACQUELINE de Vendôme .  m GUILLAUME de Mello Seigneur de Bligny, son of DREUX [VI] de Mello Seigneur de Saint-Bris & his wife Isabelle de Joigny Dame de Vendeuvre (-after 1486). 
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/vendome.htm#JeanVendomedied1460
