1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pierre_d%27Amboise
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre d'Amboise (1408 – 28 June 1473 in his castle of Meillant in Berry) was a French nobleman of the House of Amboise. He was a son of Hugh VIII of Amboise, who was killed at the battle of Agincourt, and of Jeanne de Guénand. On
2 CONC  his death he was buried in the nunnery of Order of Poor Ladies he had founded at Bourges. With his cousin Louis d'Amboise, he fought alongside Joan of Arc at the Siege of Orléans (January 1429).
2 CONT
2 CONT Titles and offices
2 CONT
2 CONT  Conseiller and chamberlain to Charles VII.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Governor of Touraine.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Louis XI's ambassador to Rome.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Lord of Chaumont, Meillant, Sagonne, Les Rochettes, Asnières (in Blésois), Saint-Vérain, Bussy, Preuilly, Les Bordes-Guénand, Moulins, Charenton, etc. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  He participated in the "Praguerie" under the rule of Charles VII.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He participated in the "Ligue de Bien-Public" under the rule of Louis XI, who, in reprisals, confiscated all his goods and had his main fortress at Chaumont destroyed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT On 23 August 1428 he married Anne de Bueil, Dame d'Aubijoux, daughter of Jean IV de Bueil and of Marguerite Dauphine d'Auvergne, countess of Sancerre.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 17 children, including:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Charles I of Amboise, favourite of Louis XI
2 CONT
2 CONT  Louis (1433–1503), bishop of Albi
2 CONT
2 CONT  John VII of Amboise, bishop and Duke of Langres
2 CONT
2 CONT  Jacques d'Amboise
2 CONT
2 CONT  A son (1440–1498), seigneur de Bussy, married Catherine de Saint-Belin (issue)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Georges d'Amboise (1460–1510), a cardinal and minister of state
2 CONT
2 CONT  Hugues (?–1515), seigneur d'Aubijoux, married Madeleine de Lescun, dame de Sauveterre (issue)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Pierre (?–1505), Bishop of Poitiers
2 CONT
2 CONT  Emery (?–1512), Grand-Master of the Order of Malta, head of the armies of Francis I of France on the Milan campaigns
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marie, married Jean de Hangest, seigneur de Genlis
2 CONT
2 CONT  Anne, married Jacques de Chazeron
2 CONT
2 CONT  Louise (?–1516), married Guillaume Gouffier de Boissy
2 CONT
2 CONT  Madeleine d'Amboise (1461–1497), abbess of Charenton and of Saint Menoux
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marguerite (?–1495). First married Jean Crespin, and then on 10 October 1457 Jean II de Rochechouart, baron de Mortemer
2 CONT
2 CONT  Catherine, dame de Linières, who married Baron Pierre de Castelnau-Caylus
2 CONT
2 CONT  Cardinal Georges d'Amboise (1460–1510), prime minister to Louis XII
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre de Amboise
2 CONT Birth 1408 Tours, Departement d'Indre-et-Loire, Centre, France
2 CONT Death 28 Jun 1473 (aged 64–65) Meillant, Departement du Cher, Centre, France
2 CONT Burial Couvent Sainte Claire Bourges, Departement du Cher, Centre, France
2 CONT Memorial ID 146598743 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/peter781?lang=en&n=d+amboise&p=pierre+iii
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Amboise-44
2 CONT https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q346968
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/146598743/pierre-de_amboise
