1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Louis de Bourbon (1405 – May 1486) was the third son of John I, Duke of Bourbon and Marie de Berry, Duchess d'Auvergne; Count of Montpensier, Clermont-en-Auvergne and Sancerre and Dauphin of Auvergne, brother of Ch
2 CONC arles I of Bourbon. He founded the Bourbon-Montpensier branch of the House of Bourbon, who would eventually take over the Duchy in 1505.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Family ==
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1428, he married Jeanne, Dauphine d'Auvergne, daughter and heiress of Beraud III, Dauphin d'Auvergne and Count of Clermont-en-Auvergne. After her death in 1436, he retained those titles[1] (his paternal grandmother having been 
2 CONC Anne of Auvergne, daughter of Dauphin Beraud II), and on 5 February 1442, married Gabrielle of La Tour (d. 1486), daughter of Bertrand V of La Tour, count of Auvergne and Boulogne. The couple had four children:
2 CONT Gilbert, Count of Montpensier (1443–1496) John (1445–1485) Gabrielle (1447–1516), Countess of Benon, married in 1485 Louis de la Tremoille (d. 1525), Prince of Talmond Charlotte (1449–1478), married in 1468 Wolfart van Borselen (d
2 CONC . 1487), Count of Grandpré and Earl of Buchan He was succeeded by his son Gilbert.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Links ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_I,_Count_of_Montpensier
2 CONT
2 CONT Medlands: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BOURBON.htm#_Toc207154614
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Louis I, Count of Montpensier
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis of Bourbon-Montpensier (1405 – May 1486), third son of John I, Duke of Bourbon and Marie de Berry, Duchess d'Auvergne; Count of Montpensier, Clermont-en-Auvergne and Sancerre and Dauphin of Auvergne, brother of Charles I of 
2 CONC Bourbon. He founded the Bourbon-Montpensier branch of the House of Bourbon, who would eventually take over the Duchy in 1505.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1428, he married Jeanne, Dauphine d'Auvergne, daughter and heiress of Beraud III, Dauphin d'Auvergne and Count of Clermont-en-Auvergne. After her death in 1436, he retained those titles[1] (his paternal grandmother having been 
2 CONC Anne of Auvergne, daughter of Dauphin Beraud II), and on February 5, 1442, married Gabrielle of La Tour (d. 1486), daughter of Bertrand V of La Tour, count of Auvergne and Boulogne. The couple had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert, Count of Montpensier (1443–1496)
2 CONT
2 CONT John (1445–1485)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gabrielle (1447–1516), Countess of Benon, married in 1485 Louis de la Tremoille (d. 1525), Prince of Talmond
2 CONT
2 CONT Charlotte (1449–1478), married in 1468 Wolfart van Borselen (d. 1487), Count of Grandpré and Earl of Buchan
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his son Gilbert.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ The Biographical Dictionary, Vol 4, (Longman, Brown and Green: London, 1844), 234.
2 CONT
