2 CONT *'''Nicolo Orsini, Conte di Nola1
2 CONT *'''M, #3500, b. 27 August 1331, d. 14 February 1399
2 CONT *Last Edited=26 Jun 2013
2 CONT *'''     Nicolo Orsini, Conte di Nola was born on 27 August 1331. He was the son''' of Roberto Orsini, Conte di Nola Signore di Vicovaro and Sveva del Balzo, Contessa di Soleto.2 '''He married Jeanne de Sabran''', daughter of Will
2 CONC iam de Sabran, Count of Ariano, '''in 1350 at Naples, Italy.2 He and Jeanne de Sabran were divorced in 1355.2 He married Maria del Balzo, Contessa di Soleto''', daughter of Raimondo del Balzo, Conte di Soleto and Isabella de Apia,
2 CONC  '''in 1358.2 He died on 14 February 1399 at age 67.1
2 CONT *'''     He gained the title of Conte di Nola. He held the office of Senator of Rome.1
2 CONT *'''Children of Nicolo Orsini, Conte di Nola and Maria del Balzo, Contessa di Soleto
2 CONT **Sveva Orsini+ b. 1360, d. 1404
2 CONT **Raimondo Orsini, Conte di Soleto e di Lecce, Duca di Benevento e di Bari Principe di Taranto2 b. 1361, d. 17 Jan 1406
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S130] Wikipedia, online http;//www.wikipedia.org. Hereinafter cited as Wikipedia.
2 CONT *[S3268] Hans Harmsen, "re: Chester Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 21 August 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Chester Family."
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p350.htm#i3500 ____________________
2 CONT *Orsini family
2 CONT *The Orsini family is an Italian noble family; it was one of the most influential princely families in medieval Italy and renaissance Rome. Members of the Orsini include popes Celestine III (1191–1198), Nicholas III (1277–1280),[1
2 CONC ] and Benedict XIII (1724–1730), 34 cardinals and numerous condottieri and other significant political and religious figures.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *Roberto (1295-1345), Gentile II's elder son, married to Sibilla del Balzo, daughter of the Great Senechal of the Kingdom of Naples. Among his sons, Giacomo (died 1379) was created cardinal by Gregory XI in 1371, '''while Nicola (
2 CONC August 27, 1331 - February 14, 1399) obtained the counties of Ariano and Celano. The latter was also Senator of Rome and enlarged the family territories in Lazio and Tuscany. His second son''', Raimondello Orsini del Balzo, suppor
2 CONC ted Charles III' coup d'état in Naples against Queen Joan II. Under king Ladislas he was among the few Neapolitan feudatories who were able to maintain their territorial power after the royal war against them. However, at his deat
2 CONC h in 1406 the southern Orsini fiefs were confiscated. Relationships with the royal family remained cold under Joan II; however, when Raimondello's son Giannantonio (1386-1453) sent his troops to help her against the usurpation att
2 CONC empt of James of Bourbon, he received in exchange the Principality of Taranto.
2 CONT *The links with the court increased further under Sergianni Caracciolo, Joan's lover and Great Senechal. A younger brother of Giannantonio one of Sergianni's daughters. However, the Orsini changed side when Alfonso V of Aragon sta
2 CONC rted his conquest of the Kingdom of Naples. Giannantonio was awarded with the duchy of Bari, the position of Great Connestable and an appanage of 100,000 ducati. Giannantonio remained faithful to Alfonso's heir, Ferdinand I, but w
2 CONC as killed during a revolt of nobles. Having died withouot legitimate sons, much of his were absorbed into the Royal Chamber. 
2 CONT * ....etc.
2 CONT *From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orsini_family ____________________
2 CONT *http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/orsini-nicola-conte-di-nola/
2 CONT ------------
