2 CONT a)         NICOLAS de Joinville ([1310/12?]-murdered 29 Jun 1335).  His parentage is confirmed by the 30 May 1320 charter cited above.  Conte di Sant’Angelo.  Delaborde records that Nicolas was justiciar and captain-general of Lab
2 CONC our in 1323, justiciar in 1324, and was assassinated 29 Jun 1335[753].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [1330/31?] ) JEANNE de Baux, daughter of --- ([1310/15?]-after 26 Apr 1347).  Her birth date is estimated from her husband’s estimated birth-date, bearing in mind that she had four children before he was killed.  A chart
2 CONC er dated 1339 records a lawsuit between "Jeanne de Baux comtesse de S. Angelo veuve de Nicolas de Joinville, en sa qualité de mère et tutrice de son fils Nicolas" and “Mathieu Mansella de Salerne seigneur de Plati”[754].  Jeanne Q
2 CONC ueen of Sicily confirmed the agreement between "Nicolas de Joinville" and “sa mère Jeanne de Baux, comte et comtesse de S. Angelo” concerning her dower “les châteaux de Bagnoli situé dans la principauté ultérieure...et celui de S.
2 CONC  Antonio-de-Planotnibus, dans la Capitanate” by charter dated 26 Apr 1347[755]. 
2 CONT
