1 NOTE {geni:about_me} An abstract  of the Will of Brandelis de Caumont, dated 1461, shows that Brandelis left a dowry to his daughter Jeanne, “futur épouse” of Antoine de Salignac (de Salinhaco). His wife Marguerite was still alive at t
2 CONC hat date, and so was almost certainly Jeanne’s mother: Cabinet des Titres, Chérin d’Hozier Fr. #31609 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/btv1b10080952h/f52.item 
2 CONT
2 CONT An abstract of a 1487 document  in Latin involving Johanna de Caumont, “Domina de Salanhaco” proves that Jeanne de Caumont had married Antoine de Salignac and was still alive when the document was written: ‘Volumes consacré à l’hi
2 CONC stoire de l’Ordre du Saint-Esprit, I-CXX’, BNF FR #1181.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/btv1b9001011d/f161.item
