1 NAME Hendrick /Corsselaer van Witthem/
2 GIVN Hendrick
2 SURN Corsselaer van Witthem
2 _MARNM Corsselaer van Witthem
1 NAME Hendrick III Corsselaer van Witthem, heer van Beersel
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1440
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 SEP 1515
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hendrik_III_Corsselaar
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00024706&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Hendrik was born about 1440, the son of Hendrik II van Witthem, Heer van Beersel, and Jacobe (Jacqueline) de Glymes, daughter of Johan I de Glymes, lord of Bergen-op-Zoom and Johanna van Boutershem, heiress of Bergen-op-
2 CONC Zoom and Grimberghe. On 27 January 1470 he contracted to marry Elisabeth van der Spout, dame d'Arquennes, daughter of Bernard van der Spout and Elisabeth d'Arquennes, dame d'Arquennes et du Petit-Roeulx. Hendrik and Elisabeth had 
2 CONC seven or eight children. Of these, Philippe and Isabeau would have progeny. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A nobleman of Brabant, Hendrik appeared several times representing the nobility of Brabant at the meetings of the General Estates of the Netherlands in the period 1476-1506. He sat as representative of Brabant on a special commiss
2 CONC ion to judge the chancellor of Burgundy, Guillaume Hugonet, and Guy de Brimeu, both close to Charles 'the Bold', duke of Burgundy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 6 June 1477, Marie of Burgundy proposed him as councillor of the Council of Brabant, a function he performed until his resignation in 1508. In 1484 he was one of the negotiators sent by Maximilian of Austria to the Flemish citi
2 CONC es in revolt. From that time he is mentioned in the sources as counsellor-chamberlain to Maximilian of Austria, later also to his son Philip 'the Handsome', and to Archduke Charles, the future Charles V; at the end of 1495 he was 
2 CONC a second chamberlain to Philip 'the Handsome'. He was also one of the governors of the young Archduke Charles and his first chamberlain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was above all a faithful ally of Maximilian of Austria in his struggles against Philippe de Cleves (in 1488-1489). He took up arms against the forces of Brussels in revolt, which led to the destruction of his most important pro
2 CONC perties in and around Brussels. His palace in the city was pillaged and burnt, the fortress at Beersel was besieged twice by the troops from Brussels and finally taken and destroyed; his castle-fortress at Braine-l'Alleud, and his
2 CONC  fortified mansion of Zittert at Tourneppe suffered the same fate. His total loyalty to Maximilian earned him the chain of a knight of the Golden Fleece, and other compensation in the form of positions, privileges, and exemptions 
2 CONC from taxes of various kinds. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1506 he was seen as one of the fifteen richest nobles in the Netherlands, and he was one of the guarantors for the 300,000 gold crowns that Philip 'the Handsome' promised as dowry for his sister Margaretha of Austria, duchess-w
2 CONC idow of Savoy. In 1494-95 he took part in the official entry of Philip 'the Handsome' into Louvain and Brussels. In 1496 he was a witness to the marriage of Philip 'the Handsome' and the Infanta Juana of Aragón. He travelled with 
2 CONC Maximilian of Austria to Germany, and he often accompanied Philip 'the Handsome' on his journeys in 1499-1501. In 1501 he was appointed one of six regents of the Netherlands during the time of the journey of Philip 'the Handsome' 
2 CONC to Spain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hendrik became a knight of the Golden Fleece at its 15th chapter at Malines in 1491. He was present at the chapter of the order in Brussels in 1501, where he was officially inducted as knight of the order, and at the chapter in Mi
2 CONC ddelbourg in 1505. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1483 to 1487 he was castellan of the ducal castle of Genappe, and from 1493 until his death he performed the important function of lieutenant of the fiefs of Brabant; from 1493 to 1501 he performed this function for the fiefs
2 CONC  of Malines. From 1504 until his death he was also grand forester and bailiff of the forests of Nivelles, Hazoy, Hez and Bossut. Hendrik died on 17 December 1515. He was buried beside his wife in the church of Saint Lambert at Bee
2 CONC rsel.
