0 @N6000000000337167914@ NOTE (Research):Clotilda, Saint Clotilda, Saint Pronounced As: kltild , d. 545, Frankish queen. She converted her husband, Clovis I, to Christianity and built with him in Paris the Church of the Apostles Peter and Paul, later renamed (
1 CONC 10th cent.) Sainte-Geneviève. After her husband's death she spent her life caring for the poor. Feast: June 3.
