0 @N6000000002187923804@ NOTE Chlodomer
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Chlodomer, also spelled Clodomir or Clodomer, born around 495, was the second of the four sons of Clovis I, King of the Franks. On the death of his father, in 511, he divided the kingdom of the Franks with his three brothers: Theu
1 CONC deric I, Childebert I, and Clotaire I. Although Theuderic, the eldest, had a better claim, Chlodomer divided half of the kingdom with his two other brothers. This was the Kingdom of Orléans, taken from the former kingdom of Syagri
1 CONC us. This kingdom included, most notably, the bishoprics of Tours, Poitiers and Orléans.
1 CONT
1 CONT Chlodomer married Guntheuca, with whom he had three sons: Theodebald, Gunthar, and Clodoald (later known as St Cloud).
1 CONT
1 CONT In 523-524, possibly at the instigation of his mother Clotilde, who was eager to avenge her nephew who had been assassinated by Sigismund of Burgundy, Chlodomer joined with his brothers in an expedition against the Burgundians. Af
1 CONC ter capturing Sigismund, Chlodomer returned to Orléans. However, Sigismund's brother Gondomar returned triumphantly to Burgundy at the head of the troops sent by his ally, the Ostrogothic king Theodoric the Great. There, he massac
1 CONC red the garrison the Franks had left behind.
1 CONT
1 CONT Although victorious, Chlodomer had Sigismund and his sons Gisald and Gondebaud assassinated on May 1, 524. He then led a second expedition against the Burgundians.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was killed on this expedition, in the spring or summer of the same year, at the Battle of Vézeronce. His three sons were entrusted to his mother until his widow married Clotaire I. Clotaire, however, had Chlodomer's children ki
1 CONC lled, although Clodoald managed to escape. Better known as Saint Cloud, he later became abbot of Nogent, having given up his hair, the symbol of the Frankish royalty, rather than giving up his life.
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT
1 CONT See also
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Franks (main history of Frankish kingdoms)
1 CONT     * List of Frankish Kings
1 CONT     * Merovingians
1 CONT     * History of France
0 @N6000000002322297275@ NOTE Receiving a quarter of his fathers partition, he received lands in western
1 CONT central France. In 523, he and two full brothers, Chlotar I and Childebert I,
1 CONT as allies, attacked his eastern neighbors, the Burgundians; their king,
1 CONT Sigismund, was captured and put to death, together with his family. In the
1 CONT following year, Clodomir resumed the attack, this time with his half-brother
1 CONT Theodoric I, but was killed  at the battle of Vezeronce, where king Godomer,
1 CONT Sigismund's brother, was his opponent.
0 @N6000000002244389827@ NOTE Merovingian king of Soissons from 511, receiving the old heartlands of the
1 CONT Salian Franks in modern northern France and Belgium. After the death of
1 CONT brother Clodomir in 524, Chlotar murdered his nephews and shared the kingdom
1 CONT of Orleans with the remaining brothers, Childebert I and Theodoric I. The
1 CONT deaths without heirs of the latter's grandson, Theobold in 555, and of
1 CONT Childebert in 558 brought all the Frankish lands under Chlotar's sway. He was
1 CONT ruthless and brutal and usually won in family hostilities. He died of fever.
0 @N6000000000437104380@ NOTE "Daughter of King Clovis I and Queen Clotilda. She was married off by her brothers to Amalaric, King of the Visigoths, who mistreated her because she was a Catholic (the Visigothic rulers were Arian). She sent to her brother King 
1 CONC Childebert of Paris for aide, and he quickly had Amalaric killed and asked his sisterto return to Paris with him. For some reason Chrotilda died on the journey. "@S153@
