0 @N6000000001354338131@ NOTE [blended.FTW]
1 CONT [mergebase.FTW]
1 CONT King of Metz 511-534
1 CONT Son of Clovis I, King of the Franks, he inherited Metz in 511 at his death. His son, Theudebert, was already of age when he ascended to thethrone. Early in his reign he sent his son to battle King Chlochilaich, a Dane who had inva
1 CONC ded Metz. Theuderic then aided the Thuringian King Hermanfrid against his only living brother Baderic. Baderic was defeated, but the land promised Theuderic was not given. The four sons ofClovis then all fought Sigismund and Godom
1 CONC ar, father and son Kings ofthe Burgundians. Sigismund was taken prisoner, and Theuderic married his daughter. Godomar was defeated, but Chlodomer, King of Orleans, was also killed in the battle.
1 CONT Theuderic then, with his brother Chlotar I and son Theudebert, attacked Thuringia to get his revenge with Hermanfrid. Thuringia was conquered, and Chlotar got Radegund, daughter of King Berthar (Harmanfrid's late brother). After m
1 CONC aking a treaty with his brother Childebert I, King of Paris, Theuderic died in 534. Upon his death the throne of Metz was up for grabs between Chlotar, Childebert, and Theudebert.
1 CONT [Fix.FTW]
