0 @N6000000002187665819@ NOTE Galswintha
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Galswintha (540-568) was the daughter of Athanagild, Visigothic king of Spain; the sister of Brunhilda, queen of Austrasia; and the wife of Chilperic I, the Merovingian king of Neustria.
1 CONT
1 CONT Galswintha and Chilperic were married at Rouen in 567, but soon afterward she was murdered at the instigation of Chilperic's mistress Fredegund, who then married him.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her death aroused the enmity of her sister Brunhild against Chilperic, brining about 40 years of warfare between the Frankish kingdoms of Austrasia and Neustria.
1 CONT
1 CONT She died in Neustria in 568.
