1 CONC dt River, spreading southward into Gaul until they reached Tournai and Cambrai. Their defeat (c. 431) by the Roman general Aetius at Helena (Hlesme), between Tournai and Cambrai, prevented further expansion. Chlodio did occupy all
1 CONC  the country as far as the Somme River, however, and he made Tournai the capital of the Salian Franks. His successor was Merovech.
1 CONT
