0 @N6000000001354335678@ NOTE [blended.FTW]
1 CONT [mergebase.FTW]
1 CONT King of the Visigoths 484-507
1 CONT After succeeding to the throne of his dead father King Euric, Alaric II proved to be a weak king. In 486 he surrendered to Clovis I, King of the Franks, Syagrius, the last Roman general in Gaul. As Alaric wasan Arian, Clovis had j
1 CONC ustification for making war. In 507, he and King Gundobad of the Burgundians attacked and defeated him. As a result,Clovis gained all of Aquitaine, reducing the land of the Visigoths toSpain. He was succeeded by his young son Amal
1 CONC aric, and Theodoric the Great, King of the Ostrogoths, was the one who ruled the kingdom in reality until 526.
1 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------  ------
