0 @N6000000001353749408@ NOTE [blended.FTW]
1 CONT [mergebase.FTW]
1 CONT King of Neustria 639-657
1 CONT King of Burgundy 639-657
1 CONT Before King Dagobert I of the Franks died, his Neustrian and Burgundian nobles urged a union of those two kingdoms, and do when he died in 639, Clovis II became king of Neustria and Burgundy. In 656, both Grimoald, Mayor of the Pa
1 CONC lace of Austrasia, and his son Childebert who he had placed on the Austrasian throne, were executed. The next year, Clovis II died, leaving the kingdom to his infant son Chlotar III, reallyjust a puppet of the powerful Neustrian a
1 CONC nd Burgundian nobles.
