0 @N6000000001744974119@ NOTE His statue is carved on his tomb at St. Denis.
1 CONT
1 CONT Energetically struggled to unite the various Frankish peoples and dominate Gaul. Clovis gradually extended his authority over almost all the tribes of Gaul. In 486, he defeated Syragius, the last Roman ruler in Gaul, then conquere
1 CONC d Gontebaud, King of the Burgundians, in 500 near Dijon, and Alaric II, King of the Visigoths, in 507 in Vouille.
1 CONT
1 CONT Urged by his wife, Clotilda, a Burgundian princess, he was baptised (with 3000 of his soldiers) into the Christain faith in Reims on Christmas Day 496 by St. Remigius. He was the only Barbarian King to have espoused the Roman Cath
1 CONC olic religion and thereafter he was supported by the Church.
1 CONT
1 CONT In accordance with the Frankish laws of succession, his kingdom was divided between his four sons after his death. They continued his expansionist policies and annexed the kingdoms of Burgundy (534 AD) and Provence (537 AD).
1 CONT
1 CONT Source: Claude Wenzler, The Kings of France (1995, Editions Ouest-France: Rennes).
1 CONT
1 CONT Another source: Church of JC of the LDS "Ancestral File" CD-Rom database, ver 4.17.
