0 @N6000000001353845681@ NOTE Theodoric III (d. 690/691), Merovingian ruler who succeeded his brother Chlotar III as king of Neustria and Burgundy in 673, at the instigation of Ebroïn, the Neustrian mayor of the palace. He was soon deposedby another brother, C
1 CONC hilderic II, was restored in 675, then was momentarily deposed
1 CONT again in favour of a certain Clovis (allegedly Chlotar III's son), but recovered his throne in 676 and finally (679) also became king of Austrasia. A puppet pure and simple, he then had to watch his subjects fight one another unti
1 CONC l the final victory of Pepin II and the Austrasians at the Battle of Tertry in 687
