0 @N6000000002187572156@ NOTE Theuderic III
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Theuderic III (or Theuderich, Theoderic, or Theodoric; in French, Thierry) (d.691) was the king of Neustria (including Burgundy) on two occassions (673 and 675-691) and king of Austrasia from 679 to his death in 691. Thus, he was 
1 CONC the king of all the Franks from 679.
1 CONT
1 CONT The son of Clovis II and Balthild, he has been described as a puppet—a roi fainéant—of Mayor of the Palace Ebroin, who may have even appointed him without the support of the nobles. He succeeded his brother Clotaire III in Neustri
1 CONC a in 673, but Childeric II of Austrasia displaced him soon thereafter until he died in 675 and Theuderic retook his throne. When Dagobert II died in 679, he received Austrasia as well and was the king of the whole Frankish realm.
1 CONT
1 CONT He and the Neustrian mayor of the palace, Waratton, made peace with Pepin of Heristal, mayor of the palace of Austrasia, in 681. However, on Waratton's death in 686, the new mayor, Berthar, made war with Austrasia and Pepin vanqui
1 CONC shed the Burgundo-Neustrian army under Berthar and Theuderic (a Neustrian) at the Battle of Tertry in 687, thus paving the way for Austrasian dominance of the Frankish state.
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT
1 CONT Family and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Clotilda, perhaps a daughter of Ansegisel and Saint Begga of Landen, and had the following children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Bertrada of Prüm (676-740)
1 CONT     * Clovis IV, king (691-695)
1 CONT     * Childebert III, king (691-695)
1 CONT
1 CONT And maybe:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Clovis III, king of Austrasia (675-676)
1 CONT     * Clotaire IV, king of Austrasia (717-719)
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT
1 CONT See also
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Franks (main history of Frankish kingdoms)
1 CONT     * List of Frankish Kings
1 CONT     * Merovingians
1 CONT     * History of France
0 @N6000000002322297651@ NOTE He succeeed his brother Chlotar III as king, but was soon deposed by brother
1 CONT Childeric II, as his crown was restored in 675, but then, "He" was deposed
1 CONT again in favor of Clovis (allegedly Chlotar's son), but recovered his crown
1 CONT in 676 and finally (679) also became King of Austrasia. A puppet pure and
1 CONT simple, he then had to watch his subjects fight one another until the final
1 CONT victory of Pepin II, and the Austrasians at the Battle of Tertry in 687. See
1 CONT message under Theodoric's wife.
