0 @N6000000002176681931@ NOTE While being held prisoner by the Black Prince of England, in England, his
1 CONT son, Charles, later Charles V, acted as regent during his captivity. Because
1 CONT he was unable to raise the required 3 million crown ransom when set free to
1 CONT do so, in 1360, John honorably resumed his captivity in England, where he
1 CONT died in 1364. He had been taken prisoner on Sep-19-1356 and forced to
1 CONT sign the disastrous treaties of 1360 during the first phases of the Hundred
1 CONT Years' War between France  & England.
