0 @N6000000002188307930@ NOTE Bonne of Bourbon
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Bonne of Bourbon (1341 – Château de Mâcon, January 19, 1402) was a daughter of Peter I, Duke of Bourbon and hence a sister of Jeanne de Bourbon.
1 CONT
1 CONT She married Count Amadeus VI of Savoy in 1355 in Paris. They had two children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Amadeus VII of Savoy (1360 - November 1, 1391). He married Bonne of Berry (1365–1435), daughter of Duke John of Berry and a niece of Bonne of Bourbon.
1 CONT     * Louis of Savoy (1362 - 1365).
0 @N6000000000337130798@ NOTE (Research):Amadeus VII Encyclop‘dia Britannica Article    born 1360, Chamb‚ry, Savoy [now in France] died Nov. 1, 1391, Ripaille byname Amadeus The Red Count,  Italian Amedeo Il Conte Rosso, French Am‚d‚e Le Comte Rouge count of S
1 CONC avoy (1383-91), during whose short rule the county of Savoy acquired Nice and other Proven‡al towns.   Son of Amadeus VI and Bonne of Bourbon, Amadeus married (1377) the daughter of Jean, duc de Berry, brother of the king of Franc
1 CONC e. His father, the "Green Count," wore his customary emerald-green livery at the wedding, and the groom earned his own sobriquet by wearing bright red. Invested with the traditional fief of Savoyard heirs apparent, the seigneury o
1 CONC f Bresse (west of Geneva), he was soon embroiled in an intermittent six-year war against a vassal, Edward of Beaujeu, who refused him homage. In 1382 he led Savoyard troops against Flemish rebels at the Battle of Rozebeke.   Amade
1 CONC us died suddenly at the castle of Ripaille, south of Lake Geneva, at the age of 31, apparently as a result of a doctor's blunder.
